lte":{"backupFileName":"426efb4feb467619@v5","version":5,"backupTime":"2026-10-08T11:33:03.598Z","realParentDir":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/src"},"packages/usage/src/UsageDashboard.svelte":{"backupFileName":"650299a2f80a2265@v21","version":21,"backupTime":"2026-10-08T12:58:33.579Z","realParentDir":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/src"},"packages/usage/src/devin.ts":{"backupFileName":"b7a86bb4452cd1ca@v2","version":2,"backupTime":"2026-10-08T11:17:12.307Z","realParentDir":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/src"},"packages/usage/src/ProviderIcon.svelte":{"backupFileName":"d25d2b7f66d62f47@v5","version":5,"backupTime":"2026-10-08T11:49:20.607Z","realParentDir":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/src"},"apps/usage/src/App.svelte":{"backupFileName":"5cb5e436277af9ce@v12","version":12,"backupTime":"2026-10-08T12:38:46.592Z","realParentDir":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/apps/usage/src"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:10:51.134Z"},"isSnapshotUpdate":false}
{"parentUuid":"e4b415a6-106b-40f5-b0b0-66ac7dcb256f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"54454a4d-12b9-4ee3-b2a6-9023849a1ade","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"proceed with the recommendation\n\nFor publishing package - create a tag based npm publish workflow similar to super functions (there is already npm token present org wide)\n\nthen add building tauri menu-bar app to linear backlog ( /use-skillplane linear-backlog-architect)\n\n\n\nAlso fix valid code review findings from these reviews:\n\n1:\n\n\n<pasted_content id=\"7934\">\nThe review finished. I didn't change any files. It found 10 issues: 4 correctness bugs, 3 problems with how the usage host handles stored sign-ins, 2 slow sequential reads, and missing or outdated docs. These are the review pass's findings; I haven't checked each one myself.\n\nCorrectness\n\n1. A failed read wipes that account's history (packages/usage/src/history.ts:54). recordUsageHistory rebuilds each account's series only from the windows in the current read. If a read fails (401, 429 with nothing cached, timeout, expired token), it comes back with windows: [] and up to 8 days of trend points for that account are deleted from usage-history.json. The comment says only removed accounts are pruned, but every temporary failure prunes too.\n2. An empty live Claude result replaces good snapshot data (apps/usage/server.mjs:109). If the OAuth endpoint returns no five_hour or seven_day windows, the result still has an observedAt time, so it wins over the status-line snapshot. The collected quota disappears, the empty result is cached for 5 minutes, and finding 1 then wipes that account's history.\n3. Concurrent preference writes can lose a change (apps/usage/accounts.mjs:338). setUsagePreferences and setDefaultClaudeDismissed each read the file, merge and write, outside writeQueue. If turning Use local sign-ins off overlaps with adding or removing a profile, the later write can put the old value back. Credential reads would then quietly resume against the user's choice.\n4. History series split when the label changes (packages/usage/src/claude-oauth.ts:116). The live reader says \"Seven-day opus quota\" and the snapshot says \"Seven-day Opus quota\". History keys include the label, so switching between live and snapshot resets that series. Swapping in harness fallback windows (server.mjs:148) does the same.\n\nStored sign-ins and the AGENTS.md exception\n\n5. Stored sign-ins are read for far more tools than the exception allows (apps/usage/server.mjs:93). AGENTS.md allows only the Claude Code and Factory Droid sign-ins and says to keep every other source on documented paths. The code also reads:\n   - Cursor's keychain token and calls DashboardService;\n   - Devin's credentials.toml and calls GetUserStatus;\n   - Pi, OpenCode, omp and Hermes tokens and calls chatgpt.com/backend-api/wham/usage and OpenCode Zen;\n   - the Antigravity OAuth token file.\n\n   The Settings text (App.svelte:541) tells the user only Claude and Factory Droid are read.\n6. /api/stored-logins ignores the off switch (apps/usage/server.mjs:283). It reads the Pi, OpenCode, omp and Hermes credential stores, including running sqlite3 and decoding token emails, even when Use local sign-ins is off. The status path checks localCredentials; this endpoint doesn't.\n7. Any website can trigger these reads (apps/usage/server.mjs:276). GET /api/status and GET /api/profiles change state but skip the origin check. A page anywhere that loads <img src=\"http://127.0.0.1:4174/api/status\"> causes:\n   - keychain prompts;\n   - live calls to Anthropic, Factory, Cursor and ChatGPT that use up rate limits and start cooldowns;\n   - history writes and possibly a new profile.\n\n   Checking Sec-Fetch-Site or requiring a custom header would block it.\n\nSpeed\n\n8. Harness logins are read one at a time, each store twice (apps/usage/server.mjs:138). With 4–8 logins, /api/status waits for the sum of all fetches (up to 15s each) instead of the slowest one. Reading each store once and running the reads in parallel fixes it.\n9. Cursor's reads also run in sequence (packages/usage/src/cursor-local.ts:97). Two independent HTTP calls and two sqlite3 reads could run together.\n\nDocs\n\n10. Docs are missing or out of date (packages/usage/README.md).\n    - There's no section naming the Superfunctions packages evaluated, which AGENTS.md requires for each new capability.\n    - The root README.md (line 5) and docs/architecture.md still say personal Cursor quota isn't supported, but cursor-local implements it.\n</pasted_content id=\"7934\">\n\n\n\n2:\n\n\n<pasted_content id=\"7934\">\nI reproduced seven functional failures using in-memory mocks, without touching credentials or settings files. I also found adapters outside the documented source exception. The review covers all 55 changed or untracked files; checks and builds pass, but they do not catch these account, permission, collector, and history issues.\nFound **8 issues**: one P1 and seven P2s.\n\n1. **\\[P1\\] Credential readers exceed the approved source boundary.** apps/usage/server.mjs:87 enables Cursor, Devin, and stored-login adapters that read credentials and call undocumented endpoints. The exception in AGENTS.md:72 permits this only for Claude Code and Factory Droid. Other providers need approved documented interfaces.\n2. **\\[P2\\] Turning local sign-ins off still reads credential stores.** apps/usage/server.mjs:281 calls all four stored-login readers without checking preferences. Opening **Add account** triggers this endpoint even with the setting disabled. Reproduced with mocked readers.\n3. **\\[P2\\] A custom default Claude directory reads the wrong sign-in.** packages/usage/src/claude.ts:37 removes `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` when it equals the host’s default—even when that default came from a custom environment override. The CLI then reads its normal default directory. The live reader also selects the default keychain service. Preserve the configured directory throughout.\n4. **\\[P2\\] Cached Claude usage gets attributed to a new account.** apps/usage/server.mjs:103 caches by profile ID, then overwrites the cached result’s identity with current auth information. Switching sign-ins within five minutes shows account A’s quota under account B’s email. Reproduced; cache entries need identity validation.\n5. **\\[P2\\] Harness fallback overrides an explicit access denial.** apps/usage/server.mjs:145 treats a blocked Codex account as eligible for fallback, replaces its state with `ok`, and clears its errors. `ordinaryUsageAllowed` remains false, producing contradictory structured status and hiding the Limited badge. Reproduced; preserve authoritative denial state.\n6. **\\[P2\\] Replacing an Antigravity collector loses the original status line.** apps/usage/accounts.mjs:457 discards another collector’s command without inheriting its saved predecessor. Install collector A over an existing status line, install B, then uninstall B: `statusLine` is deleted instead of restored. The backup is also overwritten. Reproduced with an in-memory filesystem.\n7. **\\[P2\\] One failed provider read deletes historical usage.** packages/usage/src/history.ts:44 retains history only for currently returned windows. A temporary unavailable result with `windows: []` erases that account’s entire history; temporarily omitted Claude windows have the same problem. Reproduced. Preserve prior series until retention expiry or explicit removal.\n8. **\\[P2\\] Concurrent requests bypass the single-sign-in guard.** apps/usage/accounts.mjs:540 checks for an active connection before awaiting `profiles()`, but reserves the connection afterward. Two simultaneous requests both become pending. Reproduced; serialize startup or reserve the active slot before awaiting.\n\nReviewed **7 modified tracked files and 48 untracked files**, including contracts, callers, tests, configuration, and documentation. There are no staged changes or commits ahead of the recorded upstream.\n\nValidation passed: workspace checks, non-emitting TypeScript/Svelte checks, **75 focused tests**, and current-source frontend builds performed entirely in memory. Tests requiring filesystem writes and live provider/browser checks were not run. No files, credentials, settings, or Git state were changed.\n</pasted_content id=\"7934\">\n"},"uuid":"7a42029b-fd09-4ed9-b8ce-a09bfabb6293","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:10:50.552Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":25,"turnIndex":26},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
