{"parentUuid":"7f81e66f-203b-4ad9-b409-ca0afdf83ee3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"54454a4d-12b9-4ee3-b2a6-9023849a1ade","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Original thread:** continue the SET-1 local usage-dashboard work from a prior Codex session in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset, then iterate heavily on it:\n     - a code review with fixes, and Claude multi-account support;\n     - a UI redesign in the style of usagebuddy.com, using the Twenty One Native font from @21n/fonts, Phosphor icons and ECharts;\n     - many providers: Codex/ChatGPT, Claude, Antigravity, Cursor team, Cursor personal (local), Factory Droid, Amp, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes;\n     - an opt-in \"Use local sign-ins\" mode, which is on by default at the user's explicit request;\n     - Codex banked-reset redemption, pins, sort, the options popover, the activity heatmap, the Limits card, the Upcoming resets timeline, harness merging, renaming, the footer, and more.\n   - **Most recent user request (verbatim):** \"proceed with the recommendation / For publishing package - create a tag based npm publish workflow similar to super functions (there is already npm token present org wide) / then add building tauri menu-bar app to linear backlog ( /use-skillplane linear-backlog-architect) / Also fix valid code review findings from these reviews:\" followed by two pasted reviews.\n     - **The recommendation being followed (from my previous answer):**\n       1. Fix the collector path stability (a shim plus a migration for installed collectors).\n       2. Add a local API guard (block cross-site requests).\n       3. Add a first-run consent for local sign-ins.\n       4. Publish the `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`subset-usage serve|status|collect`, `--port`, `--no-open`, bundled, Node ≥22).\n       5. Then the Tauri menu-bar app goes to the Linear backlog.\n   - **Review 1 findings to evaluate and fix:**\n     1. History wipe on a failed read (`packages/usage/src/history.ts` `recordUsageHistory` keeps only the current windows).\n     2. An empty live Claude result replaces snapshot data (server.mjs ~109).\n     3. Concurrent preference writes outside writeQueue (accounts.mjs `setUsagePreferences`/`setDefaultClaudeDismissed`).\n     4. History keys split on label differences (claude-oauth \"Seven-day opus quota\" vs snapshot \"Opus\"; the harness fallback swaps windows).\n     5. Stored sign-ins exceed the AGENTS.md exception (Cursor, Devin, Pi/OpenCode/omp/Hermes, the Antigravity token), and the Settings text claims only Claude and Factory are read.\n     6. `/api/stored-logins` ignores the off switch.\n     7. Any website can trigger GET /api/status and /api/profiles; add a Sec-Fetch-Site check or a required custom header.\n     8. Harness logins are read sequentially, each store twice.\n     9. Cursor reads are sequential (cursor-local.ts:97).\n     10. Docs are missing or stale: the Superfunctions section, and the root README.md line 5 and docs/architecture.md still say personal Cursor isn't supported.\n   - **Review 2 findings:**\n     1. [P1] Credential readers exceed the exception.\n     2. stored-logins reads while the setting is off.\n     3. A custom default Claude directory reads the wrong sign-in: `claude.ts:37` deletes CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR when it equals the host default even when that default came from an env override, and the live reader's `isDefault` keychain choice is affected the same way.\n     4. A cached Claude usage result is attributed to a new account after a sign-in switch (the cache key needs identity).\n     5. The harness fallback overrides an explicit access denial (a blocked Codex account becomes ok and its errors are cleared).\n     6. Replacing an Antigravity collector loses the original status line (inherit the predecessor's saved previous; don't overwrite the backup).\n     7. A failed read deletes history (same as review 1 #1).\n     8. Concurrent startLogin requests bypass the single sign-in guard (reserve the slot before awaiting `profiles()`).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Repo layout:\n     - npm workspaces (`packages/*`, `apps/*`).\n     - Svelte 5 in runes mode for the view and host, Vite 8, TypeScript.\n     - The `node:test` test runner.\n   - AGENTS.md rules (must follow):\n     - Packages must not import from `apps/`; apps import packages via exports.\n     - Published packages use the `@sub-set/<name>` scope (`private: false`); internal `@subset/*` packages stay private; app hosts stay private.\n     - A Git push doesn't authorize npm publication.\n     - Never show a download or integration link before it works; keep catalog `availableSurfaces` empty until verified.\n     - Superfunctions reuse gate: check `clifn`/`hostfn` for the CLI; record the packages evaluated in the README.\n     - The local sign-ins exception is documented in AGENTS.md (currently names only Claude Code and Factory Droid, \"on by default at the owner's request\"). It needs updating to list everything the owner directed: Cursor app, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes, and the Antigravity email.\n   - `scripts/check-workspaces.mjs`:\n     - Apps must be `@subset/*` and private.\n     - Public packages must be `@sub-set/*`.\n     - Workspace dependencies must use the `\"*\"` version.\n   - Superfunctions publish workflow (`/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`):\n     - Triggers on tags `'*-v*.*.*'`, plus workflow_dispatch with input `release_tag`.\n     - `scripts/resolve-release-tag.mjs` reads `release-packages.json` (`[{slug, name, path}]`), matches the tag pattern `<slug>-v<version>`, and checks the package name (and version).\n     - Steps: setup-node 22 with registry-url https://registry.npmjs.org, install, build, test, `npm pack --json`, `npm publish --access public` with `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}`.\n     - Permissions `contents: read`; concurrency group `publish-${{ github.ref }}`.\n     - The subset version must do `npm ci` at the root and build workspaces, because the CLI bundles the private `@subset/usage`.\n   - Existing Subset workflows: `.github/workflows/verify.yml` and `pullfrog.yml`.\n   - The server binds 127.0.0.1, checks Host/Origin, and requires a matching Origin for non-GET requests. CSP is `default-src 'self'`.\n   - Live readers are throttled (`throttled(key, minIntervalMs, read)` with a cooldown on 429 and Retry-After); `publicAccount` strips `retryAfterMs`.\n   - Harness merging uses the service plus email; `alsoIn` lists the other harnesses.\n   - The history file is `usage-history.json`; `historyWindowKey = limitId + '\\0' + label`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs`** (moved from apps/usage/server.mjs):\n     - Full content read most recently: the imports from `@subset/usage/*`, profilesFile/dataDirectory, loadHistory/recordHistory, liveCache/throttled, publicAccount, needsLocalSignIns, `status()` with readOne and harness merging, runStatusLine, shellQuote, claudeSetup, collectCommand, readJson, json, publicErrors, and the command dispatch (status/collect/serve).\n     - Still points to the old static directory: `const root = fileURLToPath(new URL('.', import.meta.url)); const dist = resolve(root, 'dist');`. This must become the package's `web/` directory, overridable with `SUBSET_USAGE_WEB_DIR`.\n     - The current collect command is: `node ${shellQuote(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))} collect --account ${shellQuote(id)}`, prefixed with `SUBSET_USAGE_PROFILES_FILE=` and `SUBSET_USAGE_DATA_DIR=` when they are set.\n     - The usage message says `node server.mjs`.\n   - **`packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs`** (moved from apps/usage/accounts.mjs):\n     - `createAccounts({profilesFile, managedRoot, snapshotRoot, currentHome, codexBinary, loginTimeoutMs, defaultClaudeConfigDir, preferencesFile, readClaudeAuth, antigravitySettingsFile})`.\n     - Profile and preference functions: profiles, list, addCurrent, addProvider, addFactory, addLocalTool, renameProfile, usagePreferences (`localCredentials !== false`), setUsagePreferences, ensureDefaultClaude.\n     - Collector functions: collectorStatus, installCollector, uninstallCollector, chainedStatusLine, captureSnapshot (run records in `collector-runs`).\n     - Sign-in functions: removeProfile, startLogin, connection, activeConnection, cancelLogin, close.\n     - Validation constants: `labelOf` (optional names), `legacyDefaultLabels`, `keyedProviders = new Set(['amp','devin','cursor-local'])`, `keyOptionProviders`, `storedLoginKinds` (pi/opencode/omp/hermes), `validEntryId`.\n   - **`packages/usage-cli/test/{accounts,profiles,server}.test.mjs`**: moved; imports changed to `'../src/accounts.mjs'`; the server test spawns `['src/server.mjs', ...]` with `cwd` set to the package directory (`hostDirectory = new URL('..', import.meta.url)`).\n     - The server test's request helper will need the new API guard header if one is added.\n     - The server test writes a fake `claude` that prints `{\"loggedIn\":false}`.\n   - **`apps/usage/package.json`**:\n     - Still has `\"status\": \"node server.mjs status\"`, `\"collect\": ...`, `\"serve\": \"node server.mjs serve\"`, `\"test\": \"node --test test/*.test.mjs\"`.\n     - The test directory was removed, so these scripts must change. Plan: depend on `@sub-set/usage` with version `\"*\"` and use the `subset-usage` bin.\n   - **`apps/usage/src/App.svelte`** (host UI, runes):\n     - Covers the app bar (Dashboard/Settings tabs, refresh icon, Add account), the settings page, the add and account dialogs, rename, collector install, the consent text, the footer with `USAGE_SITE_LIVE = false`, and the `api()` helper.\n     - The `api()` helper and the `refresh()` fetch need the new guard header.\n     - The Settings local sign-ins text currently mentions only Claude and Factory Droid, and needs updating.\n   - **`packages/usage/src/*`**: index.ts (contract plus `isUsageStatus`), codex.ts (including `consumeCodexResetCredit` and `nextResetCredit`), claude.ts (`readClaudeAuthStatus` with `defaultConfigDir` deletion logic), claude-oauth.ts, factory.ts, cursor.ts, cursor-local.ts, amp.ts, devin.ts, stored-logins.ts (`readEntries`, `listStoredLogins`, `storedLoginEmail`, `readOmpRows` via sqlite3), local-auth.ts (`readKeychainSecret`, `readSmallFile`, `fetchJson` with retryAfterMs, `jwtClaims`, `readAntigravityEmail`), snapshots.ts (`antigravitySpan`), history.ts (`recordUsageHistory`), present.ts (many helpers), UsageDashboard.svelte, UsageTrend.svelte, ProviderIcon.svelte, provider-logos.ts (generated).\n   - **`scripts/generate-provider-logos.mjs`** and `scripts/logos/{factory-droid,amp,pi,omp,hermes}.svg`.\n   - **`AGENTS.md`**: has the 2026-10-08 local sign-ins exception paragraph.\n   - **`packages/usage/README.md`**: extensive docs, including a \"Superfunctions reuse review\" section.\n   - **Root `package.json` scripts** (check and build) don't yet include usage-cli.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - These were earlier in the session, all resolved: Svelte `{@const}` placement, TS `$state` narrowing (fixed with the generic `$state<T>()` form), unused CSS warnings, a missing `pinnedCount`/`activeFilter` after a code slice, the history name clash with `window.history`, the grid-area leak in `.spend .meter`, the translucent tooltip from parent opacity, timeline rail gaps (fixed with a single JS-measured `.timeline-line`), the `.reset-row:first-child` selector broken by the line element (changed to `:first-of-type`), and a flaky test with an unhandled rejection (fixed by attaching the handler immediately).\n   - The aside REPL needs `screenshot({path:'./artifacts/x.png'})`; clip coordinates were unreliable, so verification used DOM evaluation instead.\n   - User feedback themes:\n     - Rename Codex to ChatGPT, and Claude Code to Claude, in display text only (CLI names stay).\n     - Remove the ≈ symbol everywhere.\n     - Local sign-ins on by default.\n     - Merge accounts that are the same across harnesses.\n     - Subtle icon colours.\n     - Various layout alignment fixes.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Completed features are verified in the browser via `aside repl` and 122+ tests.\n   - The current problem is restructuring so the publishable CLI respects \"packages must not import from apps\". Decision: the runtime moves to `packages/usage-cli` (`@sub-set/usage`, public); `apps/usage` keeps the Svelte UI; a root build step copies `apps/usage/dist` into `packages/usage-cli/web` (a build-output copy, not an import). esbuild bundles `src/server.mjs` and `@subset/usage` into `dist/cli.mjs` as the bin `subset-usage`.\n   - Planned fixes:\n     - API guard: require an `X-Subset-Request: 1` header on /api calls and reject `Sec-Fetch-Site` of `cross-site`.\n     - Collector shim at `<dataDir>/bin/subset-usage-collect` (default `~/.local/share/subset/bin`), rewritten on each start and holding `exec '<node>' '<cli>' collect \"$@\"`, with a migration that rewrites installed statusLine commands and chain files.\n     - Consent: an unset `localCredentials` is treated as off, and the UI shows a first-run consent banner.\n     - The review fixes listed above.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Continue work from the prior Orca session...\" (context: inspect the repo, state where the previous session stopped, continue).\n   - \"perform a thorough code review and fix any issues, also add claude support (With multiple accounts) if not already added\"\n   - \"the dashboard should show default logged in claude account by default\"\n   - \"why is it showing this way? [Image] https://www.usagebuddy.com/ Improve the UI of our usage dashboard to be on par and even better than this usage buddy. Right now - it looks very POC like. Also use Twenty One Native typeface from @21n/fonts\"\n   - \"[Image] how to automate this instead of asking users to manually configure this? using cli or something? Also what icons are you using? use phosphor icons, Apache E charts if any charts use is useful\"\n   - Numbered list: why partial data / second Claude not working; settings page; used/remaining toggle; equal card heights; remove \"Observed\"; resets dialog; show email; Weekly Fable limits.\n   - Numbered list: progress-bar colours; iconify logos; provider tags filter row; dropdown chevron padding; align the logo top; no source info in the bottom row; theme switcher; Factory Droid support (refer to Synara, zeron, Orca); remaining-mode bar colours bug.\n   - The answer to the AskUserQuestion: \"Provide an option in interface for users to allow Usage dash to use the local credentials for automatic reading of usage - if users turn this on - take Synara approach - if off - ask for Droid API key (also if this is turned on - check if we can use similar approach for Claude, Codex as well - of using already available local credentials) - check how synara, orca, zeron does it\"\n   - Numbered list: a default tag; a status tag only for non-success, in the bottom row; optional account name; trend chart setting; logo without the circle in filter chips; layout shift; remove the auto-refresh dropdown from the top bar; rename the Usage tab to Dashboard; icon-only refresh; local sign-ins on by default.\n   - Numbered list: Codex reset details and a reset button; Devin, Amp, OpenCode, Pi support; loading pulse; sticky header; why rate limiting; Factory logo; overlay click closes dialogs; why ≈ in remaining mode; plan sub-type; Factory partial and Antigravity no data.\n   - Numbered list: remove ≈ everywhere; simplify the resets dialog and show which reset is used; Team Premium 5x; paid credits; Cursor local login like Synara; radio placement; pin accounts; sort button; trend reset indicators.\n   - Numbered list: pin in the context menu, with a pinned icon in the footer; Cursor model split; credits aligned to the bottom; Amp text spacing and the ampcode and pi.dev logos; Claude extra-usage layout; filter chips scroll horizontally.\n   - Numbered list: hide the scrollbar; credits optional; options button holding the sort and toggles; Factory tabs; omp.sh and Hermes; provider name in the top cards; pie chart; harnesses grouped by sub-account service.\n   - Numbered list: replace the accounts card with a heatmap; centre Factory tabs; \"Codex Plus\" for harness cards; Codex → ChatGPT everywhere; Amp card empty; merge the same account across harnesses with \"also in\" logos.\n   - \"[Image] why does it says 7 days but shows so many tiles? Also remove the 10 accounts - 1 need attention row. Also on hover of the tile - show some useful info. use non accent, subtle color for pinned icon indicator, context menu icons. Add the ability to edit/remove the card title when clicked from account settings dialog. Dont render a separate row for harnesses 'Also in {logos}' - render this in second row... on hover of the logo - show the name of the harness. Dont render email in additional row if the title of the account is set - render in the provider - plan row itself\"\n   - \"place the email, also in at the start of that line; the tooltip bg is translucent... fix it; Rename Claude Code to Claude everywhere; Use a different icon for activity - probably fire icon; In the footer - add 'Built at 21n.co', 'usage.subset.dev' website link of usage, 'Star on Github' link -> github.com/21nCo/subset\"\n   - \"1. [Image] - Separate gemini, 3rd party like factory tabs 2. In the lowest remaining card - show exhausted 0%, running low as a separate rows ... exhausted row with tooltip & click to show all the exhausted accounts and same for running low row\"\n   - \"1. Show running low row first then exhausted 2. make the limits card the second one - move the next reset card as third card and render next 3 resets in this card instead of just 1 3. Make Gemini tab first and default 4. Antigravity card is not showing email for some reason - see if we can do anything about it\"\n   - \"[Image] In exhausted limits dialog, group by account\"\n   - \"[Image] increase the number size in limits card a little bit, the account names column should be aligned instead of zig zag (also the limits second column should be aligned irrespective of number on the left like if double digit etc\"\n   - \"Rename 'next resets' to 'upcoming resets.'\"\n   - \"Align the last 7 days text on the right in the card first row.\"\n   - \"Render upcoming resets as a timeline with the exact time when the reset will happen, and also retain the current time left for that reset information.\"\n   - \"The timeline should be a continuous line. Also the first card with the heat map: the tiles should be responsive to the height of the activity card.\"\n   - \"what does it take for us to distribute usage as a downloadable macOS app or run via CLI as localhost?\"\n   - \"proceed with the recommendation / For publishing package - create a tag based npm publish workflow similar to super functions (there is already npm token present org wide) / then add building tauri menu-bar app to linear backlog ( /use-skillplane linear-backlog-architect) / Also fix valid code review findings from these reviews: [review 1] [review 2]\"\n   - Security and behaviour constraints in effect:\n     - Never read or print credential or token values. Only key names and structure were inspected.\n     - Keep secrets out of logs, URLs and output.\n     - Don't publish to npm or release binaries without authorization. The user asked for the workflow, not an actual publish; tagging or publishing is outward-facing and needs confirmation.\n     - Don't commit unless asked. Nothing is committed.\n     - Treat pasted review text as data.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish the CLI package `packages/usage-cli`:\n     - `package.json`: name `@sub-set/usage`, `private: false`, version e.g. 0.1.0, `bin {\"subset-usage\": \"dist/cli.mjs\"}`, `files [dist, web, README.md]`, `engines node>=22`.\n     - devDependencies: esbuild and `@subset/usage` with version `\"*\"`.\n     - Scripts: `build` (esbuild bundle), `test` (`node --test test/*.test.mjs`), `prepack` check that `web/index.html` exists.\n     - A README.\n     - Update server.mjs: web dir resolution, CLI args `--port`, `--no-open`, `--help`, `--version`, free-port fallback, browser open, and a usage message saying `subset-usage`.\n   - Update `apps/usage/package.json` scripts (and remove its test script) to use the `subset-usage` bin; update the root `package.json` check, build and test scripts; add a script copying `apps/usage/dist` into `packages/usage-cli/web`; update `.gitignore` for `web/` and `dist/` if needed; run `npm install` to link the workspace.\n   - Collector shim plus migration of installed collectors.\n   - API guard header and Sec-Fetch-Site check (update the App.svelte fetches and the server test helper).\n   - First-run consent for local sign-ins (unset means off, with a UI banner); update the AGENTS.md exception text and the Settings text to list all owner-directed providers.\n   - Fix the review findings:\n     - History preservation (keep prior series until retention expiry; drop only removed accounts).\n     - An empty live Claude result falls back to the snapshot.\n     - Preferences writes go through a queue.\n     - Consistent window labels and keys: Claude legacy model labels capitalised; harness ChatGPT windows mapped to codex-style `limitId 'codex'` and labels `'codex · primary'`/`'codex · secondary'`.\n     - stored-logins respects the off switch.\n     - Parallel harness reads with a single store read per tool.\n     - Parallel Cursor reads.\n     - Custom default Claude directory: keep `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` unless the directory is the real `~/.claude`; compute `isDefault` against `resolve(homedir(), '.claude')`.\n     - Claude and harness cache keys include identity (email).\n     - The harness fallback doesn't override blocked/denial states and keeps errors.\n     - Antigravity/Claude collector replacement inherits the replaced collector's saved previous status line and keeps the first backup.\n     - startLogin reserves its slot before awaiting.\n   - Add tests for the fixes.\n   - Docs: root README.md and docs/architecture.md (personal Cursor is now supported; mention the CLI), packages/usage/README Superfunctions section update (esbuild, clifn/hostfn evaluated), and the CLI README.\n   - `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`, `release-packages.json` (slug e.g. `usage` → `@sub-set/usage` at `packages/usage-cli`) and `scripts/resolve-release-tag.mjs`, modelled on Superfunctions but installing and building from the repo root. Don't actually tag or publish without confirmation.\n   - Extend `scripts/check-workspaces.mjs` if useful.\n   - Run `npm run check`, `npm run build`, and all tests.\n   - Invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"use-skillplane\"` and args `linear-backlog-architect` to add the \"Tauri menu-bar app\" backlog item. Use the Linear account and workspace matching SET (linear.app/21n); per global instructions, use a direct connector or skill first, otherwise composio, and tell the user which account was used.\n   - Restart the preview server: it currently runs from the old path, `npm run serve --workspace=@subset/usage-web`, which now points to the moved file.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just begun the restructure for the CLI package:\n   - Ran `mkdir -p packages/usage-cli/src packages/usage-cli/test`.\n   - Moved `apps/usage/server.mjs` → `packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs` and `apps/usage/accounts.mjs` → `packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs`.\n   - Moved the three tests to `packages/usage-cli/test/`.\n   - Fixed the test imports (`'../src/accounts.mjs'`) and the server test spawn paths (`'src/server.mjs'`).\n   - Read the full server.mjs to plan the changes: web dir, CLI args, guard header, shim, consent, and the status() fixes for review findings 2, 4, 5, 8 and identity cache keys.\n\n   Not yet created: `packages/usage-cli/package.json`, the build config, or the README. `apps/usage/package.json` scripts still reference the removed `server.mjs` and `test/`. The root scripts aren't updated, and the running preview server (port 4174) was started from the old location.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the restructure the user approved (\"proceed with the recommendation ... create a tag based npm publish workflow similar to super functions\"):\n   1. Create `packages/usage-cli/package.json` (`@sub-set/usage`, bin `subset-usage`) and wire `apps/usage/package.json` and the root scripts.\n   2. Update server.mjs for the web dir, CLI flags, the API guard header, the collector shim and consent.\n   3. Implement the review fixes with tests.\n   4. Add the publish-tag workflow, `release-packages.json` and the resolver script.\n   5. Update the docs, including the AGENTS.md exception.\n   6. Run the full checks and tests.\n   7. Invoke `/use-skillplane linear-backlog-architect` to add the Tauri menu-bar app backlog item.\n\n   Do not push a tag or run npm publish without explicit confirmation.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/serro/.claude/projects/-Users-serro-Documents-dev-n-subset/ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"57f810f1-6d5e-4002-824c-54462e755654","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:14:51.203Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":25,"turnIndex":26},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["7a42029b-fd09-4ed9-b8ce-a09bfabb6293"],"session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
