{"parentUuid":"64494d99-ce7b-4501-a741-51b9e321170f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"54454a4d-12b9-4ee3-b2a6-9023849a1ade","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xu1gZPdemapGFnfphvshTE","type":"tool_result","content":"43:    { id: 'factory-droid', title: 'Factory Droid', detail: 'Rate limits from a local sign-in or API key' },\n83:  let localCredentials = $state(true);\n107:  // Display preferences are per-viewer conveniences, so browser storage is enough.\n169:  async function api(path: string, method = 'GET', body?: object) {\n170:    const response = await fetch(path, {\n190:      const response = await fetch('/api/status', { cache: 'no-store' });\n235:    try { localCredentials = (await api('/api/preferences')).localCredentials === true; } catch { /* keeps the default, off */ }\n241:      localCredentials = (await api('/api/preferences', 'PUT', { localCredentials: value })).localCredentials === true;\n512:            <div><h2>Auto-refresh</h2><p>Reads every account on an interval while this tab is visible. ChatGPT, Cursor, and Factory Droid are read live. Claude is read live with local sign-ins on; otherwise it and Antigravity reload their last collected snapshot.</p></div>\n542:              <p>On by default. Reads the Claude and Factory Droid sign-ins already stored on this computer to show live usage without a collector or API key. Subset reads the stored tokens without changing or refreshing them, and calls the usage endpoints those CLIs use, which their makers do not document and may change. macOS may ask to allow keychain access; choose Always Allow. ChatGPT accounts use the Codex CLI's own app-server either way.</p>\n544:            <button type=\"button\" role=\"switch\" class=\"switch\" aria-checked={localCredentials} aria-label=\"Use local sign-ins\" disabled={savingLocal} onclick={() => setLocalCredentials(!localCredentials)}><span></span></button>\n607:        <p class=\"hint\">{localCredentials ? 'Reads the account signed in to the Cursor app on this computer.' : 'Turn on local sign-ins in Settings to read the Cursor app sign-in.'} For team spending across members, use Cursor team instead.</p>\n610:          <span class=\"label\">API key environment variable <em>{newProvider === 'amp' || localCredentials ? 'optional' : 'required while local sign-ins are off'}</em></span>\n612:          <small id=\"tool-help\">{newProvider === 'amp' ? 'Leave empty to use the account amp is signed in to. For another saved account, set its Amp API key in the usage server environment and enter the variable name.' : localCredentials ? 'Leave empty to use the key stored by devin auth login. For another account, enter the name of a variable holding its key.' : 'Local sign-ins are off, so enter the name of a variable holding a Devin API key.'}</small>\n617:          {#if !localCredentials}<p class=\"hint\">Turn on local sign-ins in Settings to read logins stored by {providerMeta[newProvider].name}.</p>{/if}\n631:          <span class=\"label\">API key environment variable <em>{localCredentials ? 'optional' : 'required while local sign-ins are off'}</em></span>\n633:          <small id=\"factory-help\">{localCredentials ? 'With local sign-ins on, Subset reads the Droid sign-in in this Factory home. ' : 'Local sign-ins are off, so Subset needs a Factory API key: set it in the usage server environment and enter only the variable name. '}Use a separate Factory home per account, started with <code>FACTORY_HOME_OVERRIDE</code>.</small>\n654:        <button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn primary\" disabled={actionBusy || (newProvider === 'cursor' && (!credentialEnv.trim() || !cursorUserId.trim())) || (newProvider === 'factory-droid' && !localCredentials && !factoryKeyEnv.trim()) || (newProvider === 'devin' && !localCredentials && !factoryKeyEnv.trim()) || (isHarness(newProvider) && (!localCredentials || !storedLogin)) || (newProvider === 'cursor-local' && !localCredentials)}>\n703:              <strong>{localCredentials ? 'Local sign-in' : selectedProfile.apiKeyConfigured ? 'API key' : 'Needs an API key or local sign-ins'}</strong>\n704:              <p>{localCredentials ? `Reads the Droid sign-in stored in ${selectedProfile.factoryHome}/.factory${selectedProfile.apiKeyConfigured ? ', falling back to the API key' : ''}.` : selectedProfile.apiKeyConfigured ? 'Reads rate limits with the Factory API key from the configured variable.' : 'Turn on local sign-ins in Settings, or add this account again with an API key variable.'}</p>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"27fe4d37-5003-4930-862e-639d379c2cdc","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:20:05.763Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"43:    { id: 'factory-droid', title: 'Factory Droid', detail: 'Rate limits from a local sign-in or API key' },\n83:  let localCredentials = $state(true);\n107:  // Display preferences are per-viewer conveniences, so browser storage is enough.\n169:  async function api(path: string, method = 'GET', body?: object) {\n170:    const response = await fetch(path, {\n190:      const response = await fetch('/api/status', { cache: 'no-store' });\n235:    try { localCredentials = (await api('/api/preferences')).localCredentials === true; } catch { /* keeps the default, off */ }\n241:      localCredentials = (await api('/api/preferences', 'PUT', { localCredentials: value })).localCredentials === true;\n512:            <div><h2>Auto-refresh</h2><p>Reads every account on an interval while this tab is visible. ChatGPT, Cursor, and Factory Droid are read live. Claude is read live with local sign-ins on; otherwise it and Antigravity reload their last collected snapshot.</p></div>\n542:              <p>On by default. Reads the Claude and Factory Droid sign-ins already stored on this computer to show live usage without a collector or API key. Subset reads the stored tokens without changing or refreshing them, and calls the usage endpoints those CLIs use, which their makers do not document and may change. macOS may ask to allow keychain 