t notice()}\n\"\"\",\"\"\"{#snippet notice()}\n  {#if localCredentialsChosen === false}\n    <div class=\"banner\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Local sign-ins\">\n      <div>\n        <strong>Read the sign-ins already on this computer?</strong>\n        <p>Subset can show live usage from the logins Claude, Factory Droid, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes keep locally, and the Antigravity account email. Tokens are read, never changed or sent anywhere except each provider's own usage endpoint. You can change this in Settings.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"banner-actions\">\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn primary\" disabled={savingLocal} onclick={() => setLocalCredentials(true)}>Use local sign-ins</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" disabled={savingLocal} onclick={() => setLocalCredentials(false)}>Not now</button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  {/if}\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"<p>On by default. Reads the Claude and Factory Droid sign-ins already stored on this computer to show live usage without a collector or API key. Subset reads the stored tokens without changing or refreshing them, and calls the usage endpoints those CLIs use, which their makers do not document and may change. macOS may ask to allow keychain access; choose Always Allow. ChatGPT accounts use the Codex CLI's own app-server either way.</p>\"\"\",\"\"\"<p>Reads the sign-ins Claude, Factory Droid, the Cursor app, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes already store on this computer, and the Antigravity account email, to show live usage without a collector or API key. Subset reads the stored tokens without changing or refreshing them, and calls the usage endpoints those tools use, which their makers do not document and may change. macOS may ask to allow keychain access; choose Always Allow. ChatGPT accounts use the Codex CLI's own app-server either way.</p>\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Local sign-ins turned\" src/App.svelte","description":"Add head