{"parentUuid":"46a1a565-e4cc-41f5-b954-ecbb5330f75c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpqgiHRojGEJuy3SUrb4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5612,"cache_read_input_tokens":161784,"output_tokens":2886,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5612,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2886,"cache_read_input_tokens":161784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5612,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5612},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":647,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfpqghz4hTMV3U54zK57N","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d63b1e1-d825-4dc6-8951-c675ca2123d8","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:21:48.295Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"1d63b1e1-d825-4dc6-8951-c675ca2123d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpqgiHRojGEJuy3SUrb4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sjg9w5U8MWXF3RHYHKKTCT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:60])\n        s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('AGENTS.md',[(\"\"\"Exception, directed by the repository owner on 2026-10-08: the local usage host has a **Use local sign-ins** setting, on by default at the owner's request and visible in Settings. Only while it is on may it read the Claude Code and Factory Droid sign-ins already stored on that computer (keychain or credential files), read-only, and call the usage endpoints those CLIs use. It must never refresh, write, log, or return those tokens, and the UI must say the endpoints are undocumented. Keep every other source on documented paths.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Exception, directed by the repository owner on 2026-10-08: the local usage host has a **Use local sign-ins** setting. It stays off until the user answers a first-run question on the dashboard, and can be changed in Settings. Only while it is on may it read, read-only, the sign-ins these tools already store on that computer (keychain, credential files, or their own state databases): Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes, plus the Antigravity CLI's signed-in email. It may call only the usage endpoints those tools use. It must never refresh, write, log, or return those tokens; it must not list stored logins while the setting is off; and the UI must name these tools and say the endpoints are undocumented. Adding a tool to this list needs the owner's direction and an update here. Keep every other source on documented paths.\"\"\")])\nedit('README.md',[(\"\"\"The local usage preview supports isolated Codex/ChatGPT connections, separately collected Claude Code and Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, and authorized Cursor team-member spending reports. Personal Cursor subscription quota is not supported; neither pilot is released.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"The local usage dashboard supports isolated Codex/ChatGPT connections, Claude Code and Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, Cursor team-member spending, and, with opt-in local sign-ins, live usage for Claude, personal Cursor, Factory Droid, Devin, Amp, and logins stored by Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. It runs as the `subset-usage` CLI (`@sub-set/usage`, prepared for npm but not yet published); neither pilot is released.\"\"\")])\nedit('docs/architecture.md',[\n(\"\"\"Its sources are ChatGPT-signed-in Codex homes through the documented local app-server protocol, independently collected Claude Code/Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, and authorized Cursor team-member spending through its official Admin API. Quota snapshots and spending caps remain distinct; personal Cursor subscriptions and API billing are not implemented quota sources.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Its sources are ChatGPT-signed-in Codex homes through the documented local app-server protocol, independently collected Claude Code/Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, authorized Cursor team-member spending through its official Admin API, and, only with the opt-in local sign-ins setting (see AGENTS.md), the stored sign-ins of Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app (personal plan usage), Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. Quota snapshots and spending caps remain distinct; API billing is not an implemented quota source. The local host runtime ships as the `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`packages/usage-cli`), which bundles `@subset/usage` and the built `apps/usage` view; a tag `usage-v<version>` runs `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`.\"\"\"),\n])\nedit('packages/usage/README.md',[\n(\"\"\"The standalone host is `apps/usage`.\"\"\",\"\"\"The standalone host is the `subset-usage` CLI in `packages/usage-cli` (`@sub-set/usage`), which serves the view built from `apps/usage`.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"**Settings → Use local sign-ins** is on by default (the repository owner's choice) and stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json`; turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins. When on:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Use local sign-ins** stays off until the user answers the dashboard's first-run question; the answer is stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json` and can be changed in Settings. Turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins, including listing the logins Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes hold. When on, it also covers the Cursor app, Devin, those four harnesses, and the Antigravity email (see AGENTS.md). For example:\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"After `npm run build`, use `npm run status --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for structured JSON or `npm run serve --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for the local view at `http://127.0.0.1:4174`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"After `npm run build`, use `npm run status --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for structured JSON or `npm run serve --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for the local view at `http://127.0.0.1:4174`. Both run the `@sub-set/usage` CLI from source; see its [README](../usage-cli/README.md) for `subset-usage serve|status|collect`.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"The server binds only to `127.0.0.1`, checks Host and Origin headers, and requires a matching browser Origin for account mutations.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"The server binds only to `127.0.0.1`, checks Host and Origin headers, requires an `X-Subset-Request: 1` header on every API call (which a cross-site page cannot send without a CORS preflight the server never approves), refuses requests the browser marks `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site` or `same-site`, and requires a matching browser Origin for account mutations.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    \"command\": \"node /absolute/path/to/subset/apps/usage/server.mjs collect --account claude_example\\\"\"\"\",\n\"\"\"    \"command\": \"'/Users/you/.local/share/subset/bin/subset-usage-collect' --account 'claude_example'\\\"\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces.\"\"\",\"\"\"Collectors call a shim, `<data dir>/bin/subset-usage-collect` (default `~/.local/share/subset/bin`), that `subset-usage serve` rewrites on each start to point at the current CLI, so upgrading or moving the install does not break installed status lines. On start, the server also rewrites collectors installed with an older command, but only where the settings still hold the exact recorded collector. When one collector replaces another account's collector in a shared settings file (Antigravity), it inherits the status line that collector had replaced, and `settings.json.subset-backup` keeps the first pre-collector copy. Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"Run `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage` and `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage-web` after the package build,\"\"\",\"\"\"Run `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage` and `npm run test --workspace=@sub-set/usage` after the package build,\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"The package is private. A future npm release requires the `@sub-set/` scope, versioned exports, a release process, and separate verification.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"The 2026-10-08 CLI packaging reviewed `clifn/core` (`@clifn/core@0.1.0`, published) and `hostfn`. The CLI has three commands and four flags, so `@clifn/core`'s parser-agnostic runner and output helpers would add a runtime dependency without removing meaningful code; `hostfn` deploys hosted applications and does not cover a loopback-only local tool. Neither is used. The bundle uses `rolldown@1.2.11`, already in the workspace through Vite, as a build-time dependency only. The release workflow is modelled on Superfunctions' `publish-tag.yml` and `resolve-release-tag.mjs`.\n\nThis package stays private; `@sub-set/usage` bundles it. Publishing that CLI is a separate, verified release step.\"\"\"),\n])\nEOF\ngrep -n \"For example:\" packages/usage/README.md | head -2","description":"Update AGENTS, README, architecture, usage README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5612,"cache_read_input_tokens":161784,"output_tokens":2886,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5612,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2886,"cache_read_input_tokens":161784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5612,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5612},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Sjg9w5U8MWXF3RHYHKKTCT":{"command":"cd /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:60])\n        s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('AGENTS.md',[(\"\"\"Exception, directed by the repository owner on 2026-10-08: the local usage host has a **Use local sign-ins** setting, on by default at the owner's request and visible in Settings. Only while it is on may it read the Claude Code and Factory Droid sign-ins already stored on that computer (keychain or credential files), read-only, and call the usage endpoints those CLIs use. It must never refresh, write, log, or return those tokens, and the UI must say the endpoints are undocumented. Keep every other source on documented paths.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Exception, directed by the repository owner on 2026-10-08: the local usage host has a **Use local sign-ins** setting. It stays off until the user answers a first-run question on the dashboard, and can be changed in Settings. Only while it is on may it read, read-only, the sign-ins these tools already store on that computer (keychain, credential files, or their own state databases): Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes, plus the Antigravity CLI's signed-in email. It may call only the usage endpoints those tools use. It must never refresh, write, log, or return those tokens; it must not list stored logins while the setting is off; and the UI must name these tools and say the endpoints are undocumented. Adding a tool to this list needs the owner's direction and an update here. Keep every other source on documented paths.\"\"\")])\nedit('README.md',[(\"\"\"The local usage preview supports isolated Codex/ChatGPT connections, separately collected Claude Code and Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, and authorized Cursor team-member spending reports. Personal Cursor subscription quota is not supported; neither pilot is released.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"The local usage dashboard supports isolated Codex/ChatGPT connections, Claude Code and Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, Cursor team-member spending, and, with opt-in local sign-ins, live usage for Claude, personal Cursor, Factory Droid, Devin, Amp, and logins stored by Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. It runs as the `subset-usage` CLI (`@sub-set/usage`, prepared for npm but not yet published); neither pilot is released.\"\"\")])\nedit('docs/architecture.md',[\n(\"\"\"Its sources are ChatGPT-signed-in Codex homes through the documented local app-server protocol, independently collected Claude Code/Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, and authorized Cursor team-member spending through its official Admin API. Quota snapshots and spending caps remain distinct; personal Cursor subscriptions and API billing are not implemented quota sources.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Its sources are ChatGPT-signed-in Codex homes through the documented local app-server protocol, independently collected Claude Code/Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, authorized Cursor team-member spending through its official Admin API, and, only with the opt-in local sign-ins setting (see AGENTS.md), the stored sign-ins of Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app (personal plan usage), Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. Quota snapshots and spending caps remain distinct; API billing is not an implemented quota source. The local host runtime ships as the `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`packages/usage-cli`), which bundles `@subset/usage` and the built `apps/usage` view; a tag `usage-v<version>` runs `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`.\"\"\"),\n])\nedit('packages/usage/README.md',[\n(\"\"\"The standalone host is `apps/usage`.\"\"\",\"\"\"The standalone host is the `subset-usage` CLI in `packages/usage-cli` (`@sub-set/usage`), which serves the view built from `apps/usage`.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"**Settings → Use local sign-ins** is on by default (the repository owner's choice) and stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json`; turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins. When on:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Use local sign-ins** stays off until the user answers the dashboard's first-run question; the answer is stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json` and can be changed in Settings. Turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins, including listing the logins Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes hold. When on, it also covers the Cursor app, Devin, those four harnesses, and the Antigravity email (see AGENTS.md). For example:\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"After `npm run build`, use `npm run status --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for structured JSON or `npm run serve --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for the local view at `http://127.0.0.1:4174`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"After `npm run build`, use `npm run status --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for structured JSON or `npm run serve --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for the local view at `http://127.0.0.1:4174`. Both run the `@sub-set/usage` CLI from source; see its [README](../usage-cli/README.md) for `subset-usage serve|status|collect`.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"The server binds only to `127.0.0.1`, checks Host and Origin headers, and requires a matching browser Origin for account mutations.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"The server binds only to `127.0.0.1`, checks Host and Origin headers, requires an `X-Subset-Request: 1` header on every API call (which a cross-site page cannot send without a CORS preflight the server never approves), refuses requests the browser marks `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site` or `same-site`, and requires a matching browser Origin for account mutations.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    \"command\": \"node /absolute/path/to/subset/apps/usage/server.mjs collect --account claude_example\\\"\"\"\",\n\"\"\"    \"command\": \"'/Users/you/.local/share/subset/bin/subset-usage-collect' --account 'claude_example'\\\"\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces.\"\"\",\"\"\"Collectors call a shim, `<data dir>/bin/subset-usage-collect` (default `~/.local/share/subset/bin`), that `subset-usage serve` rewrites on each start to point at the current CLI, so upgrading or moving the install does not break installed status lines. On start, the server also rewrites collectors installed with an older command, but only where the settings still hold the exact recorded collector. When one collector replaces another account's collector in a shared settings file (Antigravity), it inherits the status line that collector had replaced, and `settings.json.subset-backup` keeps the first pre-collector copy. Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"Run `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage` and `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage-web` after the package build,\"\"\",\"\"\"Run `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage` and `npm run test --workspace=@sub-set/usage` after the package build,\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"The package is private. A future npm release requires the `@sub-set/` scope, versioned exports, a release process, and separate verification.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"The 2026-10-08 CLI packaging reviewed `clifn/core` (`@clifn/core@0.1.0`, published) and `hostfn`. The CLI has three commands and four flags, so `@clifn/core`'s parser-agnostic runner and output helpers would add a runtime dependency without removing meaningful code; `hostfn` deploys hosted applications and does not cover a loopback-only local tool. Neither is used. The bundle uses `rolldown@1.2.11`, already in the workspace through Vite, as a build-time dependency only. The release workflow is modelled on Superfunctions' `publish-tag.yml` and `resolve-release-tag.mjs`.\n\nThis package stays private; `@sub-set/usage` bundles it. Publishing that CLI is a separate, verified release step.\"\"\"),\n])\nEOF\ngrep -n \"For example:\" packages/usage/README.md | head -2","description":"Update AGENTS, README, architecture, usage README"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Sjg9w5U8MWXF3RHYHKKTCT":{"cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfpqghz4hTMV3U54zK57N","type":"assistant","uuid":"20be1f50-8368-4fc2-adf0-e888bc0202d1","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:22:09.381Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"20be1f50-8368-4fc2-adf0-e888bc0202d1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Sjg9w5U8MWXF3RHYHKKTCT","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -z \"${HOME-}\" ]; then case \"${OSTYPE-}\" in msys*|cygwin*|win32*) printf '{}\\n'; if [ -z \"${ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_PORT-}\" ] || [ -z \"${ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_TOKEN-}\" ] || [ -z \"${ORCA_PANE_KEY-}\" ]; then exit 0; fi; { command -p cat 2>/dev/null || cat; } >/dev/null 2>&1 || : ;; *) { command -p cat 2>/dev/null || cat; } >/dev/null 2>&1 || :; printf '{}\\n' ;; esac; else case \"${OSTYPE-}\" in msys*|cygwin*|win32*) if [ -f \"${HOME-}/.orca/agent-hooks/claude-hook.cmd\" ]; then case \"${HOME-}\" in *\\&*|*\\^*|*\\(*|*\\)*|*\\;*|*,*|*=*|*%*|*\\!*) if [ -f \"${SYSTEMROOT-}/System32/WindowsPowerShell/v1.0/powershell.exe\" ]; then \"${SYSTEMROOT-}/System32/WindowsPowerShell/v1.0/powershell.exe\" -NoProfile -EncodedCommand ; else printf '{}\\n'; if [ -z \"${ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_PORT-}\" ] || [ -z \"${ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_TOKEN-}\" ] || [ -z \"${ORCA_PANE_KEY-}\" ]; then exit 0; fi; { command -p cat 2>/dev/null || cat; } >/dev/null 2>&1 || :; fi ;; *) \"${HOME-}/.orca/agent-hooks/claude-hook.cmd\" ;; esac; else printf '{}\\n'; if [ -z \"${ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_PORT-}\" ] || [ -z \"${ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_TOKEN-}\" ] || [ -z \"${ORCA_PANE_KEY-}\" ]; then exit 0; fi; { command -p cat 2>/dev/null || cat; } >/dev/null 2>&1 || :; fi ;; *) if [ -f \"${HOME-}/.orca/agent-hooks/claude-hook.sh\" ] && [ -r \"${HOME-}/.orca/agent-hooks/claude-hook.sh\" ] && [ -x \"${HOME-}/.orca/agent-hooks/claude-hook.sh\" ]; then ORCA_HOOK_AGENT_PID=\"${PPID:-}\"; export ORCA_HOOK_AGENT_PID; /bin/sh \"${HOME-}/.orca/agent-hooks/claude-hook.sh\"; else { command -p cat 2>/dev/null || cat; } >/dev/null 2>&1 || :; printf '{}\\n'; fi ;; esac; fi","durationMs":58},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0b9fc442-30e8-492e-bd55-ddcce7cfb40e","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:22:09.461Z","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"20be1f50-8368-4fc2-adf0-e888bc0202d1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"54454a4d-12b9-4ee3-b2a6-9023849a1ade","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sjg9w5U8MWXF3RHYHKKTCT","type":"tool_result","content":"27:**Use local sign-ins** stays off until the user answers the dashboard's first-run question; the answer is stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json` and can be changed in Settings. Turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins, including listing the logins Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes hold. When on, it also covers the Cursor app, Devin, those four harnesses, and the Antigravity email (see AGENTS.md). For example:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7602cbab-0a70-4e99-a031-c175cf1cd162","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:22:09.724Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"27:**Use local sign-ins** stays off until the user answers the dashboard's first-run question; the answer is stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json` and can be changed in Settings. Turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins, including listing the logins Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes hold. When on, it also covers the Cursor app, Devin, those four harnesses, and the Antigravity email (see AGENTS.md). For example:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/AGENTS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":69,"oldLines":7,"newStart":69,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Distinguish provider-reported quota or reset time, locally measured token usage or cost, calculated estimates, and unavailable values. Outright's existing run usage events are one potential measured source, not proof of remaining subscription quota. Use a provider-specific adapter only with a legitimate, reliable source and clear account authorization. Use only credential paths and endpoints approved for this integration. Never claim all subscriptions are covered when only some sources are supported. Show account, source, observation time, freshness, and partial failures per provider. A browser-only app cannot read local CLI state; a local connector or authorized provider connection is required for that data."," ","-Exception, directed by the repository owner on 2026-10-08: the local usage host has a **Use local sign-ins** setting, on by default at the owner's request and visible in Settings. Only while it is on may it read the Claude Code and Factory Droid sign-ins already stored on that computer (keychain or credential files), read-only, and call the usage endpoints those CLIs use. It must never refresh, write, log, or return those tokens, and the UI must say the endpoints are undocumented. Keep every other source on documented paths.","+Exception, directed by the repository owner on 2026-10-08: the local usage host has a **Use local sign-ins** setting. It stays off until the user answers a first-run question on the dashboard, and can be changed in Settings. Only while it is on may it read, read-only, the sign-ins these tools already store on that computer (keychain, credential files, or their own state databases): Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes, plus the Antigravity CLI's signed-in email. It may call only the usage endpoints those tools use. It must never refresh, write, log, or return those tokens; it must not list stored logins while the setting is off; and the UI must name these tools and say the endpoints are undocumented. Adding a tool to this list needs the owner's direction and an update here. Keep every other source on documented paths."," "," The usage pilot's source selection and interface plan live in [SET-1](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-1/pilot-a-reusable-usage-status-dashboard) and its linked planning documents. Treat these as plans until the relevant package and host checks pass."," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":7,"newStart":2,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Subset is a collection of small, independently useful apps. Each app solves one focused problem and can, where its platform allows, also serve as a capability inside 21n products or as an interface returned by an AI agent."," ","-The first pilots are a **usage dashboard** and a **PDF annotation and review tool**. The local usage preview supports isolated Codex/ChatGPT connections, separately collected Claude Code and Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, and authorized Cursor team-member spending reports. Personal Cursor subscription quota is not supported; neither pilot is released. The directory labels availability accordingly.","+The first pilots are a **usage dashboard** and a **PDF annotation and review tool**. The local usage dashboard supports isolated Codex/ChatGPT connections, Claude Code and Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, Cursor team-member spending, and, with opt-in local sign-ins, live usage for Claude, personal Cursor, Factory Droid, Devin, Amp, and logins stored by Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. It runs as the `subset-usage` CLI (`@sub-set/usage`, prepared for npm but not yet published); neither pilot is released. The directory labels availability accordingly."," "," ## Product model"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/docs/architecture.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":7,"newStart":13,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Native delivery | Swift and platform APIs when required | Planned. Native permissions and views stay in native targets; share a stable data/operation contract where useful. |"," | Agent delivery | Structured result, optional registered view; separate local CLI/skill | Planned. Each host and the published CLI/skill require their own verification. |"," ","-The usage dashboard boundary is normalized per-source status and explicit read operations. Its sources are ChatGPT-signed-in Codex homes through the documented local app-server protocol, independently collected Claude Code/Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, and authorized Cursor team-member spending through its official Admin API. Quota snapshots and spending caps remain distinct; personal Cursor subscriptions and API billing are not implemented quota sources. The standalone host owns profile persistence and collector bindings, while the package owns normalization and source reads. Proposed consumers are a standalone web host, an Outright adapter, a local CLI and skill for shell-capable agents, and a registered view in an agent host. The PDF review boundary is document identity, page/annotation operations, and explicit export; web, native, product, and agent views may differ. No capability may import an app or a consuming product.","+The usage dashboard boundary is normalized per-source status and explicit read operations. Its sources are ChatGPT-signed-in Codex homes through the documented local app-server protocol, independently collected Claude Code/Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, authorized Cursor team-member spending through its official Admin API, and, only with the opt-in local sign-ins setting (see AGENTS.md), the stored sign-ins of Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app (personal plan usage), Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. Quota snapshots and spending caps remain distinct; API billing is not an implemented quota source. The local host runtime ships as the `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`packages/usage-cli`), which bundles `@subset/usage` and the built `apps/usage` view; a tag `usage-v<version>` runs `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`. The standalone host owns profile persistence and collector bindings, while the package owns normalization and source reads. Proposed consumers are a standalone web host, an Outright adapter, a local CLI and skill for shell-capable agents, and a registered view in an agent host. The PDF review boundary is document identity, page/annotation operations, and explicit export; web, native, product, and agent views may differ. No capability may import an app or a consuming product."," "," ## Decisions and gates"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1,"newLines":6,"lines":[" # Usage capability (SET-1)"," ","-This private package owns the version 1 per-account usage contract, read-only provider adapters, the registered view ID `subset.usage.dashboard@1`, a structured agent result with a text fallback, and the shared Svelte dashboard view. The standalone host is `apps/usage`. No public surface is released. External view inputs are validated with `isUsageStatus()` before the standalone host renders them.","+This private package owns the version 1 per-account usage contract, read-only provider adapters, the registered view ID `subset.usage.dashboard@1`, a structured agent result with a text fallback, and the shared Svelte dashboard view. The standalone host is the `subset-usage` CLI in `packages/usage-cli` (`@sub-set/usage`), which serves the view built from `apps/usage`. No public surface is released. External view inputs are validated with `isUsageStatus()` before the standalone host renders them."," "," ## Supported local sources"," "]},{"oldStart":24,"oldLines":7,"newStart":24,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## Local sign-ins (opt-in)"," ","-**Settings → Use local sign-ins** is on by default (the repository owner's choice) and stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json`; turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins. When on:","+**Use local sign-ins** stays off until the user answers the dashboard's first-run question; the answer is stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json` and can be changed in Settings. Turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins, including listing the logins Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes hold. When on, it also covers the Cursor app, Devin, those four harnesses, and the Antigravity email (see AGENTS.md). For example:"," "," - **Claude Code:** for each account bound to a config directory, the host first runs `claude auth status` (Claude Code refreshes its own token there), then reads the stored OAuth access token from the macOS keychain item `Claude Code-credentials` (default directory) or `Claude Code-credentials-<first 8 hex of SHA-256 of the directory>`, falling back to `<dir>/.credentials.json`. It calls `https://api.anthropic.com/api/oauth/usage` read-only and shows `five_hour`, `seven_day`, and `limits[]` entries of kind `weekly_scoped` (per-model weekly limits such as Fable). Subset never calls the token endpoint: Anthropic rotates refresh tokens, so refreshing would sign Claude Code out. An expired token asks the user to open Claude Code. If no stored sign-in is found, the status-line snapshot is used."," - **Factory Droid:** reads `<factory home>/.factory/auth.v2.loginkeychain`, `auth.v2.keyring`, or `auth.v2.file`, decrypts it (AES-256-GCM) with the key from the keychain item `Factory CLI` or `auth.v2.key`, and calls `https://api.factory.ai/api/billing/limits` (or the EU host) with the account's organization. When off, a Droid account needs a Factory API key variable; Subset then calls `/api/cli/whoami` for the organization and the same limits endpoint."]},{"oldStart":61,"oldLines":7,"newStart":61,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Each manually added home must already be signed in with its intended ChatGPT account using Codex. `CODEX_HOME=/absolute/path/to/personal-codex-home codex login` is the Codex-managed login path. `--profile` selects a config overlay within one home and is not account isolation. Do not copy auth files between homes. Account email is not stored in profile metadata or sent to the dashboard status view, so labels should distinguish accounts. A second real ChatGPT sign-in has not yet been available for live two-account verification."," ","-After `npm run build`, use `npm run status --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for structured JSON or `npm run serve --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for the local view at `http://127.0.0.1:4174`. `SUBSET_USAGE_PROFILES_FILE` selects a different JSON file; the existing `SUBSET_CODEX_PROFILES_FILE` remains a fallback for persisted Codex setups. The default stays `~/.config/subset/codex-profiles.json` and accepts all provider types. `SUBSET_USAGE_DATA_DIR` optionally selects a managed data directory; `SUBSET_USAGE_PORT` changes the loopback port. Stop the server with Ctrl-C or SIGTERM. The server binds only to `127.0.0.1`, checks Host and Origin headers, and requires a matching browser Origin for account mutations. This is a local preview, not a published CLI/skill, hosted agent view, or public web app. OpenAI documents Codex app-server authentication for local or open-source applications, with a different authorization path required for commercial or hosted services.","+After `npm run build`, use `npm run status --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for structured JSON or `npm run serve --workspace=@subset/usage-web` for the local view at `http://127.0.0.1:4174`. Both run the `@sub-set/usage` CLI from source; see its [README](../usage-cli/README.md) for `subset-usage serve|status|collect`. `SUBSET_USAGE_PROFILES_FILE` selects a different JSON file; the existing `SUBSET_CODEX_PROFILES_FILE` remains a fallback for persisted Codex setups. The default stays `~/.config/subset/codex-profiles.json` and accepts all provider types. `SUBSET_USAGE_DATA_DIR` optionally selects a managed data directory; `SUBSET_USAGE_PORT` changes the loopback port. Stop the server with Ctrl-C or SIGTERM. The server binds only to `127.0.0.1`, checks Host and Origin headers, requires an `X-Subset-Request: 1` header on every API call (which a cross-site page cannot send without a CORS preflight the server never approves), refuses requests the browser marks `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site` or `same-site`, and requires a matching browser Origin for account mutations. This is a local preview, not a published CLI/skill, hosted agent view, or public web app. OpenAI documents Codex app-server authentication for local or open-source applications, with a different authorization path required for commercial or hosted services."," "," ### Paid credits and extra usage"," "]},{"oldStart":85,"oldLines":7,"newStart":85,"newLines":7,"lines":[" {","   \"statusLine\": {","     \"type\": \"command\",","-    \"command\": \"node /absolute/path/to/subset/apps/usage/server.mjs collect --account claude_example\"","+    \"command\": \"'/Users/you/.local/share/subset/bin/subset-usage-collect' --account 'claude_example'\"","   }"," }"," ```"]},{"oldStart":94,"oldLines":7,"newStart":94,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," For several Claude Code accounts, use one [`CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars) per account (for example `~/.claude` and `~/.claude-work`, launched with `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude-work claude`) and enter that directory when adding the account. The host stores it as `claudeConfigDir`, requires it to be unique, and shows the launch command, the `settings.json` path, and the `statusLine` JSON for that account. The collector rejects a payload whose `transcript_path` lies under a different `<config dir>/projects/` tree, falling back to `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` in its environment when no transcript path is present. Claude Code's subprocess env scrub can remove `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, so a payload with neither signal is accepted. An account without a config directory keeps the unchecked binding. The transcript path is used only for this check and is never stored."," ","-Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces. This collector alone renders no status-line text. To retain an existing status line, use a wrapper that passes the same stdin JSON to the collector and existing renderer, without logging or persisting the raw payload. Subset edits provider settings only through the explicit install and uninstall operations above.","+Collectors call a shim, `<data dir>/bin/subset-usage-collect` (default `~/.local/share/subset/bin`), that `subset-usage serve` rewrites on each start to point at the current CLI, so upgrading or moving the install does not break installed status lines. On start, the server also rewrites collectors installed with an older command, but only where the settings still hold the exact recorded collector. When one collector replaces another account's collector in a shared settings file (Antigravity), it inherits the status line that collector had replaced, and `settings.json.subset-backup` keeps the first pre-collector copy. Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces. This collector alone renders no status-line text. To retain an existing status line, use a wrapper that passes the same stdin JSON to the collector and existing renderer, without logging or persisting the raw payload. Subset edits provider settings only through the explicit install and uninstall operations above."," "," The [Claude Code status-line contract](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/statusline#rate-limit-usage) supplies `rate_limits.five_hour` and `rate_limits.seven_day`, with `used_percentage` and epoch-second `resets_at`. These subscription fields are documented for Pro/Max after the first API response. Claude Code omits a window it has no data for and drops one after it resets, so an absent window is not reported as partial data; a present window with invalid values is. The installed Claude Code CLI uses model-scoped weekly keys such as `seven_day_opus` internally, but they are not documented for the status line. The collector keeps `seven_day_fable`, `seven_day_opus`, `seven_day_sonnet`, and `seven_day_haiku` only if the status-line JSON includes them, shown as for example \"Weekly Fable usage\". Remaining quota is calculated from reported usage, not inferred from tokens or context size."," "]},{"oldStart":112,"oldLines":7,"newStart":112,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## Validation and release gaps"," ","-Run `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage` and `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage-web` after the package build, alongside root `npm run check` and `npm run build`. Root checks build the catalog and usage declarations before checking consuming apps, so they do not require pre-existing ignored `dist` exports. Tests exercise synthetic multi-account provider reads, explicit access denials, safe transport failures, separate snapshot collection, normalization, redaction, profile persistence/removal, pending-login recovery, the local CLI, and host Origin checks. These are not proof of real upstream multi-account login, installed CLI compatibility, or live Cursor API authorization. No public or external-agent availability is claimed by these additions.","+Run `npm run test --workspace=@subset/usage` and `npm run test --workspace=@sub-set/usage` after the package build, alongside root `npm run check` and `npm run build`. Root checks build the catalog and usage declarations before checking consuming apps, so they do not require pre-existing ignored `dist` exports. Tests exercise synthetic multi-account provider reads, explicit access denials, safe transport failures, separate snapshot collection, normalization, redaction, profile persistence/removal, pending-login recovery, the local CLI, and host Origin checks. These are not proof of real upstream multi-account login, installed CLI compatibility, or live Cursor API authorization. No public or external-agent availability is claimed by these additions."," "," ## Superfunctions reuse review"," "]},{"oldStart":122,"oldLines":4,"newStart":122,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," The 2026-10-08 UI update checked the current `superfunctions-dev` checkout for icon and chart packages; none is published there, so the view uses `phosphor-svelte@3.1.0` and `echarts@6.1.0` directly as narrow presentation dependencies."," ","-The package is private. A future npm release requires the `@sub-set/` scope, versioned exports, a release process, and separate verification.","+The 2026-10-08 CLI packaging reviewed `clifn/core` (`@clifn/core@0.1.0`, published) and `hostfn`. The CLI has three commands and four flags, so `@clifn/core`'s parser-agnostic runner and output helpers would add a runtime dependency without removing meaningful code; `hostfn` deploys hosted applications and does not cover a loopback-only local tool. Neither is used. The bundle uses `rolldown@1.2.11`, already in the workspace through Vite, as a build-time dependency only. The release workflow is modelled on Superfunctions' `publish-tag.yml` and `resolve-release-tag.mjs`.","+","+This package stays private; `@sub-set/usage` bundles it. Publishing that CLI is a separate, verified release step."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/AGENTS.md","/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/README.md","/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/docs/architecture.md","/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/README.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"20be1f50-8368-4fc2-adf0-e888bc0202d1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
