{"parentUuid":"2020f501-5439-4eb8-a4a5-a04a69e56bb4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"54454a4d-12b9-4ee3-b2a6-9023849a1ade","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TfBEoqp91v4FiP94KAfBad","type":"tool_result","content":"> svelte-check --tsconfig ./tsconfig.json\n\n1791465749469 START \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/apps/usage\"\n1791465749469 COMPLETED 137 FILES 0 ERRORS 0 WARNINGS 0 FILES_WITH_PROBLEMS\n> node scripts/build.mjs\n\n# pass 93\n# fail 0\n# pass 35\n# fail 0","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2e67b6a4-505f-40eb-ae5f-08292f3ace73","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:22:39.044Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"> svelte-check --tsconfig ./tsconfig.json\n\n1791465749469 START \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/apps/usage\"\n1791465749469 COMPLETED 137 FILES 0 ERRORS 0 WARNINGS 0 FILES_WITH_PROBLEMS\n> node scripts/build.mjs\n\n# pass 93\n# fail 0\n# pass 35\n# fail 0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage-cli/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":39,"lines":["+# @sub-set/usage","+","+A local dashboard and CLI for AI subscription usage: ChatGPT (Codex), Claude, Cursor, Factory Droid, Amp, Devin, Antigravity, and logins stored by Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. It runs on your computer, binds only to `127.0.0.1`, and sends nothing to Subset.","+","+> Status: prepared for npm, not yet published. Install from a tarball or the repository until a release is announced.","+","+## Use","+","+Requires Node.js 22 or later.","+","+```sh","+npx @sub-set/usage            # open the dashboard","+npm install -g @sub-set/usage # or install the subset-usage command","+subset-usage serve --port 4174 --no-open","+subset-usage status           # current usage as JSON, read-only","+```","+","+| Command | What it does |","+| --- | --- |","+| `serve` (default) | Starts the dashboard on `127.0.0.1` (port 4174, or the next free port) and opens it. `--port <n>` requires that port; `--no-open` skips the browser. Ctrl-C stops it. |","+| `status` | Prints the normalized usage status (`@subset/usage` contract, schema version 1) and exits. |","+| `collect --account <id>` | Saves a quota snapshot from a Claude Code or Antigravity status line. Installed collectors call it through a shim; you rarely run it yourself. |","+| `--help`, `--version` | |","+","+## Data and permissions","+","+- Configuration: `~/.config/subset/codex-profiles.json` (override with `SUBSET_USAGE_PROFILES_FILE`).","+- Data: `~/.local/share/subset/` (override with `SUBSET_USAGE_DATA_DIR`): managed Codex homes, quota snapshots, usage history (times and percentages only), and the collector shim `bin/subset-usage-collect`.","+- **Use local sign-ins** is off until you choose on the dashboard's first-run question. When on, the CLI reads, without changing or refreshing, the sign-ins Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes keep on this computer, and calls the usage endpoints those tools use. Those endpoints are undocumented and may change. Tokens are never stored, logged, or sent to the page.","+- Installing a collector edits that CLI's `settings.json` only when you ask, keeps a backup, and keeps your previous status line running.","+- The local API accepts only same-origin requests carrying the dashboard's own header.","+","+## Development","+","+From the repository root, `npm run build` builds `@subset/usage`, the `apps/usage` view, and this package: `dist/cli.mjs` (bundled with rolldown, no runtime dependencies) and `web/` (a copy of `apps/usage/dist`). `npm test --workspace=@sub-set/usage` runs the CLI tests. `npm run serve --workspace=@sub-set/usage` runs the source without bundling.","+","+## Release","+","+Releases are tag-based. Bump `version` here, merge, then push a tag `usage-v<version>`; `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml` installs, checks, builds, tests, packs, and publishes with the organization `NPM_TOKEN`. `scripts/resolve-release-tag.mjs` refuses a tag whose version or package name does not match. Verify the published package (`npx @sub-set/usage@<version> --version`, then a real `serve`) before listing it as available anywhere."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":24,"oldLines":7,"newStart":24,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## Local sign-ins (opt-in)"," ","-**Use local sign-ins** stays off until the user answers the dashboard's first-run question; the answer is stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json` and can be changed in Settings. Turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins, including listing the logins Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes hold. When on, it also covers the Cursor app, Devin, those four harnesses, and the Antigravity email (see AGENTS.md). For example:","+**Use local sign-ins** stays off until the user answers the dashboard's first-run question; the answer is stored server-side in `usage-preferences.json` and can be changed in Settings. Turning it off stops all reads of stored sign-ins, including listing the logins Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes hold. When on, it also covers the Cursor app, Devin, those four harnesses, and the Antigravity email (see AGENTS.md). The Claude and Factory readers work as follows:"," "," - **Claude Code:** for each account bound to a config directory, the host first runs `claude auth status` (Claude Code refreshes its own token there), then reads the stored OAuth access token from the macOS keychain item `Claude Code-credentials` (default directory) or `Claude Code-credentials-<first 8 hex of SHA-256 of the directory>`, falling back to `<dir>/.credentials.json`. It calls `https://api.anthropic.com/api/oauth/usage` read-only and shows `five_hour`, `seven_day`, and `limits[]` entries of kind `weekly_scoped` (per-model weekly limits such as Fable). Subset never calls the token endpoint: Anthropic rotates refresh tokens, so refreshing would sign Claude Code out. An expired token asks the user to open Claude Code. If no stored sign-in is found, the status-line snapshot is used."," - **Factory Droid:** reads `<factory home>/.factory/auth.v2.loginkeychain`, `auth.v2.keyring`, or `auth.v2.file`, decrypts it (AES-256-GCM) with the key from the keychain item `Factory CLI` or `auth.v2.key`, and calls `https://api.factory.ai/api/billing/limits` (or the EU host) with the account's organization. When off, a Droid account needs a Factory API key variable; Subset then calls `/api/cli/whoami` for the organization and the same limits endpoint."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage-cli/README.md","/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/README.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2020f501-5439-4eb8-a4a5-a04a69e56bb4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
