{"parentUuid":"d36a9705-4712-4670-9ffe-05aefbd50f0b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpqzsVp8pDRzzTCbR8iR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No duplicates in the SET team. Creating a parent plus three PR-sized children in Subset → Backlog, linked to SET-1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1798,"cache_read_input_tokens":196577,"output_tokens":3118,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":122},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1798,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3118,"cache_read_input_tokens":196577,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1798},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfpqzs8yWjVZNao78ACjs","attributionSkill":"use-skillplane","type":"assistant","uuid":"6ff9830b-349d-40ff-ac2d-987c3f41a7ef","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:25:55.828Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"6ff9830b-349d-40ff-ac2d-987c3f41a7ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpqzsVp8pDRzzTCbR8iR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JwJdYEgW9LaiL6YQpMDoGE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-serro-Documents-dev-n-subset/ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe/scratchpad/linear && cd $_ && cat > issues.json <<'EOF'\n{\n\"parent\": {\"title\": \"Deliver Subset Usage as a macOS menu-bar app (Tauri)\", \"description\": \"## Outcome\\n\\nA macOS user installs a signed Subset Usage app, sees their lowest remaining AI subscription quota in the menu bar, and opens the full usage dashboard from it, without installing Node or running a terminal command.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe usage pilot (SET-1) runs today as the local `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`packages/usage-cli`: `subset-usage serve|status|collect`, loopback-only server, bundled `@subset/usage` runtime and `apps/usage` view). The tag-based npm publish workflow exists but nothing is published yet. Installed Claude/Antigravity status-line collectors call a stable shim at `~/.local/share/subset/bin/subset-usage-collect`, which `serve` rewrites to point at the current runtime.\\n\\n## Completion gate\\n\\nAll children are done, and a signed, notarized build has been installed on a clean macOS account and shows live usage from at least ChatGPT and Claude. Only then may the catalog list a macOS surface (AGENTS.md: publish only working availability). This parent is a container, not an implementation slice.\\n\\n## Exclusions\\n\\niOS, Windows, Linux tray builds; a hosted or synced version; any change to which local sign-ins are read (that list is governed by the AGENTS.md exception).\"},\n\"shell\": {\"title\": \"Run the usage runtime inside a Tauri menu-bar shell\", \"description\": \"## Behavior\\n\\nLaunching the app starts the usage runtime on 127.0.0.1 with a free port, shows a menu-bar icon, and opens the existing dashboard in a popover or window when clicked. Quitting stops the runtime and frees the port. No Dock icon by default.\\n\\n## Decision needed first\\n\\nHow the runtime ships: (a) bundle a Node 22 sidecar plus `dist/cli.mjs` and `web/` (fast, ~40-60 MB, keeps one codebase), (b) a Node single-executable app as the sidecar, or (c) port the server/readers to Rust. Recommendation: (a) or (b) now; revisit (c) only if size or startup is a problem.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nNew `native/usage-menubar/` Tauri v2 target that embeds the built `@sub-set/usage` artifacts. The collector shim must point at the bundled runtime after first launch, and existing collectors must keep working (the CLI's migration already rewrites only exact recorded collector commands). The webview loads only the loopback dashboard; the API guard header (`X-Subset-Request`) and Host/Origin checks stay in force.\\n\\n## Acceptance evidence\\n\\n- Launch, open, close, and quit on macOS 15+ with no orphaned runtime process (checked with `lsof`/`ps`).\\n- Port collision falls back to a free port.\\n- An installed Claude collector keeps collecting after switching from the CLI to the app.\\n- Keychain prompts for local sign-ins name the app and \\\"Always Allow\\\" persists across relaunch; document the identity change from the CLI's `node` binary.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nManual macOS run recorded in the PR, plus a scripted smoke test that starts the bundled sidecar and checks `/api/status` with the guard header.\"},\n\"tray\": {\"title\": \"Show usage status in the menu-bar icon and menu\", \"description\": \"## Behavior\\n\\nThe menu-bar item shows the lowest remaining percentage (or an alert glyph when a window is exhausted or an account needs attention). Its menu lists each account's provider, name or email, remaining percent, and next reset, plus Refresh, Open dashboard, Settings, and Quit. It refreshes on the dashboard's auto-refresh interval and pauses while the Mac sleeps.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nReads the existing `status` contract (`@subset/usage` schema version 1) from the runtime; no new provider reads and no credentials in the menu. Respects the used/remaining display preference. Stale or failed reads show their observation time and error instead of old numbers presented as current.\\n\\n## Acceptance evidence\\n\\n- Exhausted, running-low, stale, and failed-read states each render distinctly (fixture-driven test).\\n- VoiceOver reads the menu items; keyboard navigation works.\\n- Light and dark menu bars render the template icon correctly.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\nBlocked by the Tauri shell issue (needs the running runtime and port).\"},\n\"release\": {\"title\": \"Sign, notarize, and release the macOS menu-bar app\", \"description\": \"## Behavior\\n\\nA user downloads a DMG from a verified link, opens it without Gatekeeper warnings, and receives later versions through an update check.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nDeveloper ID signing and notarization in CI, a tag-based release (parallel to the npm `publish-tag.yml`), checksums, Tauri updater feed, and catalog metadata. The download link and the catalog's macOS surface are added only after a clean-machine install passes.\\n\\n## Acceptance evidence\\n\\n- `spctl --assess` and `stapler validate` pass on the released artifact.\\n- Install on a clean macOS user account, first launch, local sign-ins consent, live usage shown.\\n- Update from version N to N+1 succeeds and keeps settings, history, and collectors.\\n- Release notes, version, checksum, and catalog entry agree.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\nBlocked by the Tauri shell and menu-bar status issues. Requires Apple Developer ID credentials as CI secrets (owner action).\"}\n}\nEOF\ncat > create.mjs <<'EOF'\nconst spec = JSON.parse(await Bun.file('issues.json').text());\nconst team = '4a1900cb-d310-48d5-948e-4bd239d520fe', project = 'b3952e5a-6468-410b-8a20-314221965afe', backlog = '9d5a2319-51e8-492d-b293-5595073d38f2';\nconst q = async (query, variables = {}) => {\n  const r = await execute('LINEAR_RUN_QUERY_OR_MUTATION', { query_or_mutation: query, variables });\n  const data = r?.data?.data ?? r?.data;\n  if (r?.data?.errors) throw new Error(JSON.stringify(r.data.errors));\n  return data;\n};\nconst create = async (key, parentId) => {\n  const { title, description } = spec[key];\n  const d = await q('mutation($input: IssueCreateInput!) { issueCreate(input: $input) { success issue { id identifier url } } }',\n    { input: { teamId: team, projectId: project, stateId: backlog, title, description, ...(parentId ? { parentId } : {}) } });\n  const issue = d.issueCreate.issue;\n  console.log(key, issue.identifier, issue.url);\n  return issue;\n};\nconst out = {};\nout.parent = await create('parent');\nawait Bun.write('created.json', JSON.stringify(out));\nfor (const key of ['shell', 'tray', 'release']) { out[key] = await create(key, out.parent.id); await Bun.write('created.json', JSON.stringify(out)); }\nconst block = async (blocker, blocked) => q('mutation($input: IssueRelationCreateInput!) { issueRelationCreate(input: $input) { success } }', { input: { issueId: blocker.id, relatedIssueId: blocked.id, type: 'blocks' } });\nawait block(out.shell, out.tray);\nawait block(out.shell, out.release);\nawait block(out.tray, out.release);\nawait q('mutation($input: IssueRelationCreateInput!) { issueRelationCreate(input: $input) { success } }', { input: { issueId: out.parent.id, relatedIssueId: '6636ac93-4cb9-4c03-82b1-b2bd50b968ba', type: 'related' } });\nconsole.log('relations done');\nEOF\ncomposio run -f create.mjs --account 21n 2>&1 | grep -v RUN_LOG | tail -12","description":"Create Linear parent, children, and relations","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1798,"cache_read_input_tokens":196577,"output_tokens":3118,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":122},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1798,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3118,"cache_read_input_tokens":196577,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1798},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JwJdYEgW9LaiL6YQpMDoGE":{"command":"mkdir -p /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-serro-Documents-dev-n-subset/ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe/scratchpad/linear && cd $_ && cat > issues.json <<'EOF'\n{\n\"parent\": {\"title\": \"Deliver Subset Usage as a macOS menu-bar app (Tauri)\", \"description\": \"## Outcome\\n\\nA macOS user installs a signed Subset Usage app, sees their lowest remaining AI subscription quota in the menu bar, and opens the full usage dashboard from it, without installing Node or running a terminal command.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe usage pilot (SET-1) runs today as the local `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`packages/usage-cli`: `subset-usage serve|status|collect`, loopback-only server, bundled `@subset/usage` runtime and `apps/usage` view). The tag-based npm publish workflow exists but nothing is published yet. Installed Claude/Antigravity status-line collectors call a stable shim at `~/.local/share/subset/bin/subset-usage-collect`, which `serve` rewrites to point at the current runtime.\\n\\n## Completion gate\\n\\nAll children are done, and a signed, notarized build has been installed on a clean macOS account and shows live usage from at least ChatGPT and Claude. Only then may the catalog list a macOS surface (AGENTS.md: publish only working availability). This parent is a container, not an implementation slice.\\n\\n## Exclusions\\n\\niOS, Windows, Linux tray builds; a hosted or synced version; any change to