glyph when a window is exhausted or an account needs attention). Its menu lists each account's provider, name or email, remaining percent, and next reset, plus Refresh, Open dashboard, Settings, and Quit. It refreshes on the dashboard's auto-refresh interval and pauses while the Mac sleeps.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nReads the existing `status` contract (`@subset/usage` schema version 1) from the runtime; no new provider reads and no credentials in the menu. Respects the used/remaining display preference. Stale or failed reads show their observation time and error instead of old numbers presented as current.\\n\\n## Acceptance evidence\\n\\n- Exhausted, running-low, stale, and failed-read states each render distinctly (fixture-driven test).\\n- VoiceOver reads the menu items; keyboard navigation works.\\n- Light and dark menu bars render the template icon correctly.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\nBlocked by the Tauri shell issue (needs the running runtime and port).\"},\n\"release\": {\"title\": \"Sign, notarize, and release the macOS menu-bar app\", \"description\": \"## Behavior\\n\\nA user downloads a DMG from a verified link, opens it without Gatekeeper warnings, and receives later versions through an update check.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nDeveloper ID signing and notarization in CI, a tag-based release (parallel to the npm `publish-tag.yml`), checksums, Tauri updater feed, and catalog metadata. The download link and the catalog's macOS surface are added only after a clean-machine install passes.\\n\\n## Acceptance evidence\\n\\n- `spctl --assess` and `stapler validate` pass on the released artifact.\\n- Install on a clean macOS user account, first launch, local sign-ins consent, live usage shown.\\n- Update from version N to N+1 succeeds and keeps settings, history, and collectors.\\n- Release notes, version, checksum, and catalog entry agree.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\nBlocked by the Tauri shell and menu-bar status issues. Requires Apple Developer ID credentials as CI secrets (owner action).\"}\n}\nEOF\ncat > create.mjs <<'EOF'\nconst spec = JSON.parse(await Bun.file('issues.json').text());\nconst team = '4a1900cb-d310-48d5-948e-4bd239d520fe', project = 'b3952e5a-6468-410b-8a20-314221965afe', backlog = '9d5a2319-51e8-492d-b293-5595073d38f2';\nconst q = async (query, variables = {}) => {\n  const r = await execute('LINEAR_RUN_QUERY_OR_MUTATION', { query_or_mutation: query, variables });\n  const data = r?.data?.data ?? r?.data;\n  if (r?.data?.errors) throw new Error(JSON.stringify(r.data.errors));\n  return data;\n};\nconst create = async (key, parentId) => {\n  const { title, description } = spec[key];\n  const d = await q('mutation($input: IssueCreateInput!) { issueCreate(input: $input) { success issue { id identifier url } } }',\n    { input: { teamId: team, projectId: project, stateId: backlog, title, description, ...(parentId ? { parentId } : {}) } });\n  const issue = d.issueCreate.issue;\n  console.log(key, issue.identifier, issue.url);\n  return issue;\n};\nconst out = {};\nout.parent = await create('parent');\nawait Bun.write('created.json', JSON.stringify(out));\nfor (const key of ['shell', 'tray', 'release']) { out[key] = await create(key, out.parent.id); await Bun.write('created.json', JSON.stringify(out)); }\nconst block = async (blocker, blocked) => q('mutation($input: IssueRelationCreateInput!) { issueRelationCreate(input: $input) { success } }', { input: { issueId: blocker.id, relatedIssueId: blocked.id, type: 'blocks' } });\nawait block(out.shell, out.tray);\nawait block(out.shell, out.release);\nawait block(out.tray, out.release);\nawait q('mutation($input: IssueRelationCreateInput!) { issueRelationCreate(input: $input) { success } }', { input: { issueId: out.parent.id, relatedIssueId: '6636ac93-4cb9-4c03-82b1-b2bd50b968ba', type: 'related' } });\nconsole.log('relations done');\nEOF\ncomposio run -f create.mjs --account 21n 2>&1 | grep -v RUN_LOG | tail -12","description":"Create Linear parent, children, and relations","ti