{"parentUuid":"c37c8fc5-0769-4121-b55b-938eff90dcb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpr63SFTEeKBoFtX8Xa3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":758,"cache_read_input_tokens":201760,"output_tokens":1995,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":147},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":758,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1995,"cache_read_input_tokens":201760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":758},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8217,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfpr6379RabSqJCfJEVSU","attributionSkill":"use-skillplane","type":"assistant","uuid":"0fcdd40c-fd15-4e5f-b1d3-466c32084531","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:27:12.426Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"0fcdd40c-fd15-4e5f-b1d3-466c32084531","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpr63SFTEeKBoFtX8Xa3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything you asked for is done. `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass, and all 128 tests pass (93 library, 35 CLI). Nothing is committed, tagged or published.\n\n**CLI package `@sub-set/usage`** (in `packages/usage-cli`)\n- The server and account code moved here from `apps/usage`, so packages no longer import from apps. `apps/usage` now holds only the Svelte UI. The CLI's build bundles the shared `@subset/usage` code into `dist/cli.mjs` and copies the built UI into `web/`.\n- It needs Node 22 or later and has no runtime dependencies. I bundled with rolldown, which Vite already brings in, instead of adding esbuild.\n- Commands: `subset-usage serve|status|collect`, with `--port`, `--no-open`, `--help` and `--version`. The default port is 4174 and moves to the next free port if that one is taken.\n- I tested a packed tarball installed into a scratch prefix: the page loads, an API call without the new header is refused, and the collector shim is written.\n- Status-line collectors now call a stable shim at `~/.local/share/subset/bin/subset-usage-collect`. `serve` rewrites it on each start, and also updates collectors installed with an older command, but only where the settings file still holds that exact collector.\n  - **This already ran on your machine:** your `~/.claude/settings.json` status line now calls the shim. It had pointed at `apps/usage/server.mjs`, which no longer exists.\n- Two security changes:\n  - **API guard:** every API call needs an `X-Subset-Request: 1` header, and requests the browser marks as cross-site or same-site are refused.\n  - **First-run consent:** local sign-ins stay off until the user answers a question on the dashboard. Your saved choice (on) is unchanged. The banner itself wasn't checked in a browser, because your machine already has a saved answer.\n- The preview is running again at `http://127.0.0.1:4174`. All 10 cards read OK with your real accounts, and the ChatGPT card shows OpenCode, omp and Pi as \"also in\".\n\n**Publish workflow**\n- `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml` follows the Superfunctions one: a tag like `usage-v0.1.0` triggers it, and you can also run it by hand.\n- It installs and builds from the repo root, because the CLI bundles private workspace code.\n- It then checks, tests, packs and publishes using the org `NPM_TOKEN` secret.\n- The tag-checking script refuses a version or package-name mismatch, or a package not marked public.\n- `scripts/check-workspaces.mjs` now also checks that public packages are listed in `release-packages.json` and don't depend at runtime on private workspaces.\n\n**Review findings:** I fixed every finding from both reviews:\n- **Failed reads:** a failed read no longer erases history. An empty live Claude result falls back to the collected snapshot.\n- **Fewer reads:** each tool's login store is read once per refresh. Harness and Cursor reads now run in parallel.\n- **Concurrency:** preference writes are queued. Two sign-ins can no longer start at once.\n- **Account identity:** cached results are keyed by the signed-in email, so switching sign-ins can't show the previous account's numbers.\n  - The harness fallback no longer overrides an account Codex reports as blocked, and keeps its errors.\n  - A custom default Claude directory now gets its own sign-in.\n- **Collectors:** replacing another account's collector keeps your original status line, and the first settings backup is preserved.\n- **Trend history keys:** labels are now consistent across sources.\n- **Local sign-ins:**\n  - The stored-logins list returns nothing while local sign-ins are off.\n  - The exception text in `AGENTS.md`, the Settings copy and the docs now name every tool that's read: Claude, Factory Droid, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes and the Antigravity email.\n\n**Linear** (21n account, Subset team and project, all in Backlog)\n- [SET-14](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-14/deliver-subset-usage-as-a-macos-menu-bar-app-tauri) is the parent, linked to SET-1 as related.\n- [SET-15](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-15/run-the-usage-runtime-inside-a-tauri-menu-bar-shell) runs the usage server inside a Tauri menu-bar shell. It needs a decision first: ship Node alongside the app, or port the server to Rust.\n- [SET-16](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-16/show-usage-status-in-the-menu-bar-icon-and-menu) shows usage in the menu-bar icon and menu. It's blocked by SET-15.\n- [SET-17](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-17/sign-notarize-and-release-the-macos-menu-bar-app) covers signing, notarization and release. It's blocked by SET-15 and SET-16, and needs Apple Developer ID credentials.\n- I read the parent, blocking and related links back from Linear and they're correct.\n- I couldn't read the team's setting for auto-closing parent issues; the API returned null. So check that SET-14 can't close itself before the clean-machine install check in its description has passed.\n\nTo release, merge this work and push the tag `usage-v0.1.0`. Then verify `npx @sub-set/usage@0.1.0` before listing it anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":758,"cache_read_input_tokens":201760,"output_tokens":1995,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":147},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":758,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1995,"cache_read_input_tokens":201760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":758},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfpr6379RabSqJCfJEVSU","attributionSkill":"use-skillplane","type":"assistant","uuid":"21dec8dd-c565-40bb-a542-d60761114935","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:27:22.416Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
