{"parentUuid":"2927bcca-eba5-41be-ab0e-287752152920","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"You asked me to package the usage dashboard as a publishable CLI, add a tag-based npm workflow, fix the review findings, and add a Tauri menu-bar backlog. That's all done and the checks pass. Next, you merge and push the tag `usage-v0.1.0` to publish.","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:30:28.186Z","uuid":"239d0d8d-d35d-4f03-abc8-77323235ce7b","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"239d0d8d-d35d-4f03-abc8-77323235ce7b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d43e326-7ee1-41e3-ad41-37cb97bf8598","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"fix the valid rereview findings:\n\n1:\n\n\n<pasted_content id=\"7934\">\nI re-ran the review on the current working tree. Since the last pass the code has moved into a new packages/usage-cli package, and there's now a publish workflow and release scripts. Nine of the ten earlier findings are fixed. The tenth was resolved by changing AGENTS.md instead of the code, and that change is now the top finding. Nothing was edited.\n\nEarlier findings\n\nI checked these against the code myself:\n1. History wiped on a failed read: fixed. History now starts from what's already recorded, so an empty read no longer deletes anything.\n2. Empty Claude result replacing the snapshot: fixed. The live result is only used if it has windows or the snapshot has none (server.mjs:122).\n3. Unserialized preference writes: fixed. They now go through their own write queue (accounts.mjs:85).\n4. \"opus\" vs \"Opus\" label: fixed. The live labels are now capitalized to match the snapshot.\n5. Stored sign-ins for unapproved tools: see the first new finding below.\n6. /api/stored-logins ignoring the off switch: fixed. It returns nothing while local sign-ins are off.\n7. Cross-site GET requests: fixed. Every /api/ request now needs an x-subset-request header and is refused when Sec-Fetch-Site is cross-site or same-site.\n8. Harness logins read one at a time: fixed. They're now read in parallel.\n9. Cursor reads one at a time: fixed. They're now read in parallel.\n10. Docs: fixed. The usage README has a Superfunctions section, and the root README and docs/architecture.md now describe Cursor support.\n\nNew findings\n\nMost important\n1. AGENTS.md was rewritten to permit the new readers (AGENTS.md:72). The exception the owner directed covered only the Claude Code and Factory Droid sign-ins, on by default. The diff extends it to Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes and Antigravity, and turns the setting off by default (accounts.mjs:349). The new text also says adding a tool \"needs the owner's direction\". Only you can confirm whether the owner actually directed this; if not, those readers break the rule.\n2. A retried \"use a reset\" can spend a second Codex reset (apps/usage/src/App.svelte:320). Each click makes a new idempotency key. If the first request succeeds but its response is lost, clicking again redeems another reset. Keeping the same key for retries of the same action fixes it.\n3. status isn't read-only (packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:84). status() calls ensureDefaultClaude(), which can add a claude_default profile, and it also writes usage-history.json. AGENTS.md requires status --json to be read-only.\n\nWrong account shown\n4. Harness logins are grouped by email alone (packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:152). Logins for different ChatGPT workspaces under the same email (say, Personal and Team) collapse into one card. One workspace's quota disappears, or its numbers show on the other card.\n5. The Factory local sign-in overrides a profile's configured key (packages/usage/src/factory.ts:131). When local sign-ins are on, a profile set up with account B's key shows account A's limits. Devin uses the opposite order, so the two providers behave inconsistently.\n6. Devin falls back to the default sign-in when the profile's key is missing (packages/usage/src/devin.ts:82). If the profile's key variable isn't set, it uses the default local login instead. The \"Work\" card then shows the personal account's quota as OK rather than an error.\n7. Antigravity accounts share one settings.json (packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:408). Installing one account's collector replaces the other's, and the dashboard's \"Reinstall\" button just swaps them back. Only one account ever collects.\n\nSmaller issues\n8. Stale results after changing settings (App.svelte:190). refresh() does nothing if a refresh is already running. Turning on local sign-ins or using a reset mid-refresh can leave old results on screen until the next auto-refresh, up to 30 minutes later.\n9. claude auth status runs on every refresh (server.mjs:111). It runs once per Claude profile, with a timeout of up to 10 seconds, even when local sign-ins are off and the result isn't used. It isn't cached.\n10. An option name doesn't match (accounts.mjs:57). readClaudeAuth passes defaultConfigDir, but the reader only accepts builtInConfigDir, so the option is silently ignored. server.mjs also works out the default Claude directory separately, so the two can drift apart.\n</pasted_content id=\"7934\">\n\n\n\n2:\n\n\n<pasted_content id=\"7934\">\nThe original eight findings are resolved in the scenarios reported. I found related account-identity gaps plus new CLI and release issues, with mocked reproductions confirming the runtime cases. All 63 reviewed file hashes still match the starting snapshot.\nFound five actionable issues:\n\n1. **\\[P1\\] Manual releases can publish a different commit from the requested tag.** .github/workflows/publish-tag.yml:30 checks out the dispatch ref, while `release_tag` only selects and validates the package version. Dispatching from `main` can publish untagged changes under an existing release version. Checkout and verify the requested tag before building.\n2. **\\[P2\\] Old Claude snapshots can be attributed to a newly signed-in account.** packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:113 adds the current auth email to previously collected quota. After switching accounts, disabling local sign-ins or losing live credentials returns the old account’s windows under the new email. A mocked reproduction confirmed this. Bind snapshots to the observed identity or invalidate them when identity changes.\n3. **\\[P2\\] Cache identity checks remain incomplete.** packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:107 uses an empty identity when a stored login lacks an email. Replacing that login still returns the previous quota for two minutes; account IDs, token changes, and sign-out flags are ignored. Other provider caches also remain keyed only by profile. Validate the current credential state before cache reuse and use a stable account identity.\n4. **\\[P2\\] Separate profile configurations overwrite each other’s collector shim.** packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:208 uses one shim per data directory but embeds the active profiles-file path. Starting configuration B overwrites the shim already installed for A, redirecting A’s collectors to B’s profiles. A mocked reproduction confirmed the overwrite. Give each configuration its own shim or preserve its binding in the collector command.\n5. **\\[P2\\] The advertised read-only `status` command persists configuration.** packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:84 calls `ensureDefaultClaude()`, which writes an automatically discovered profile. Keep discovery transient for `status`, or reserve persistence for an explicit account operation.\n\nAll eight previous findings were rechecked. The revised provider authorization, disabled-store listing, custom Claude directory selection, original live-cache mismatch, blocked fallback, collector restoration, history retention, and concurrent-login cases are resolved.\n</pasted_content id=\"7934\">\n"},"uuid":"2cf8ceae-8714-49ae-b744-5bc6be155954","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:47:16.765Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":26,"turnIndex":27},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
