{"parentUuid":"2c746960-b724-4cd5-8089-394aa00f7eb6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpsz5ULqAKdVBK4i8ukh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014USPG1LJ9qGeiHMNQ5buEx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:70])\n        s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('packages/usage-cli/README.md',[\n(\"\"\"| `status` | Prints the normalized usage status (`@subset/usage` contract, schema version 1) and exits. |\"\"\",\"\"\"| `status` | Prints the normalized usage status (`@subset/usage` contract, schema version 1) and exits. It writes nothing: a signed-in default Claude account is shown without being saved, and no history is recorded. |\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"and the collector shim `bin/subset-usage-collect`.\"\"\",\"\"\"and the collector shim `bin/subset-usage-collect` (`bin/subset-usage-collect-<hash>` for a custom profiles file, so configurations sharing a data directory keep separate collectors).\"\"\"),\n])\nedit('packages/usage/README.md',[\n(\"\"\"Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces.\"\"\",\"\"\"Antigravity keeps one `settings.json`, so only one Antigravity account can collect at a time: installing for a second account is refused while another account's collector is installed there, and that account's settings say which account holds it. Claude snapshots carry no identity, so the host records the email `claude auth status` reports for each account (`claude-identities.json` in the data directory); after a sign-in change, snapshots observed earlier are not shown under the new account. Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"- **Codex** is unchanged:\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Configured keys win:** a Factory Droid or Devin account set up with an API key variable always reads that key's account and reports an error when the variable is unset, rather than falling back to the default local sign-in.\n- **Harness logins** (Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes) are grouped by email and ChatGPT workspace, and join a direct ChatGPT account only when the plans agree, so a Personal and a Team workspace under one email stay separate. Cached reads are keyed by a hash of the stored login, so a replaced login is read again at once.\n- **Codex** is unchanged:\"\"\"),\n])\nEOF\nnpm run check 2>&1 | grep -E \"COMPLETED|rror\" | head; npm run build 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error\" | head; npm test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^# (pass|fail)\"","description":"Update docs and run check, build, tests","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_read_input_tokens":253453,"output_tokens":1038,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":71},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":829,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1038,"cache_read_input_tokens":253453,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":829},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014USPG1LJ9qGeiHMNQ5buEx":{"command":"cd /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:70])\n        s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('packages/usage-cli/README.md',[\n(\"\"\"| `status` | Prints the normalized usage status (`@subset/usage` contract, schema version 1) and exits. |\"\"\",\"\"\"| `status` | Prints the normalized usage status (`@subset/usage` contract, schema version 1) and exits. It writes nothing: a signed-in default Claude account is shown without being saved, and no history is recorded. |\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"and the collector shim `bin/subset-usage-collect`.\"\"\",\"\"\"and the collector shim `bin/subset-usage-collect` (`bin/subset-usage-collect-<hash>` for a custom profiles file, so configurations sharing a data directory keep separate collectors).\"\"\"),\n])\nedit('packages/usage/README.md',[\n(\"\"\"Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces.\"\"\",\"\"\"Antigravity keeps one `settings.json`, so only one Antigravity account can collect at a time: installing for a second account is refused while another account's collector is installed there, and that account's settings say which account holds it. Claude snapshots carry no identity, so the host records the email `claude auth status` reports for each account (`claude-identities.json` in the data directory); after a sign-in change, snapshots observed earlier are not shown under the new account. Use the generated command verbatim when paths contain spaces.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"- **Codex** is unchanged:\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Configured keys win:** a Factory Droid or Devin account set up with an API key variable always reads that key's account and reports an error when the variable is unset, rather than falling back to the default local sign-in.\n- **Harness logins** (Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes) are grouped by email and ChatGPT workspace, and join a direct ChatGPT account only when the plans agree, so a Personal and a Team workspace under one email stay separate. Cached reads are keyed by a hash of the stored login, so a replaced login is read again at once.\n- **Codex** is unchanged:\"\"\"),\n])\nEOF\nnpm run check 2>&1 | grep -E \"COMPLETED|rror\" | head; npm run build 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error\" | head; npm test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^# (pass|fail)\"","description":"Update docs and run check, build, tests","timeout":600000}}