{"parentUuid":"c1d0a29e-891a-4d00-a851-4857a1c88101","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpt2aAKEejfDQvKq6Hd9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":255544,"output_tokens":1377,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1377,"cache_read_input_tokens":255544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8113,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfpt2ZrhsMZ7AzEDrMCbx","type":"assistant","uuid":"f3148139-f673-4b05-a5f7-24b28d9ac06a","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:52:39.045Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"f3148139-f673-4b05-a5f7-24b28d9ac06a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpt2aAKEejfDQvKq6Hd9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed every valid finding from both re-reviews. One needs your confirmation rather than a code change: the AGENTS.md exception (re-review 1, finding 1). `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass, and all 129 tests pass (93 library, 36 CLI). Your live dashboard still shows the same 10 accounts with no errors, and nothing is committed or tagged.\n\n**Needs your confirmation: AGENTS.md exception.** I widened it last round because you asked for those readers in this conversation: personal Cursor, Devin, Amp, Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes, and the Antigravity email. The change to \"off until the user answers a first-run question\" came from my recommendation, which you approved, though you had earlier asked for \"on by default\". If either isn't what you want, tell me and I'll revert that part.\n\n**Fixed:**\n- **Manual publish could use the wrong commit:** a manual run of `publish-tag.yml` now checks out the requested tag. It also fails unless the checked-out commit is that tag's commit.\n- **`status` wasn't read-only:** it now writes nothing. A signed-in default Claude account is shown without being saved, and no history or sign-in records are written. The dashboard server still saves these as before.\n- **A retried Codex reset could spend a second reset:** a retry now reuses the same idempotency key until a response arrives, for up to 10 minutes.\n- **Different workspaces under one email were merged:** harness logins (Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes) are now grouped by email *and* ChatGPT workspace. They join a direct ChatGPT card only when the plans match, so Personal and Team stay separate. That workspace and plan come from the stored login's token, read locally.\n- **Factory and Devin used the wrong account:** an account set up with an API key variable now always uses that key. If the variable isn't set, it shows an error instead of quietly reading your default local sign-in.\n- **Antigravity accounts swapped collectors:** Antigravity has one settings file, so a second account's collector install is now refused. That account shows \"Used by another account\" instead of offering a Reinstall that swaps them.\n- **Old Claude snapshots shown under a new account:** the server now records which email each Claude account was signed in as, in `claude-identities.json`. After a sign-in change, earlier snapshots aren't shown under the new account; the card says it's waiting for a new snapshot.\n- **Stale cached results after replacing a stored login:** harness results are now cached against a hash of the stored login (account, workspace and token), so a replaced or signed-out login is read again immediately.\n- **Two configurations overwrote each other's collector shim:** a custom profiles file now gets its own shim (`subset-usage-collect-<hash>`). Your default setup keeps `subset-usage-collect`.\n- **Stale results after changing settings:** a refresh requested while another is running now runs once more afterwards.\n- **`claude auth status` on every refresh:** results are now cached per directory for 60 seconds. It still runs when local sign-ins are off, because its result supplies the card's email and signed-in state.\n- **Option name mismatch:** the ignored `defaultConfigDir` option is removed. The built-in `~/.claude` directory is now defined in one place.\n\n**Not fully fixed:** the Factory, personal Cursor, Devin and Amp caches are still keyed by account only. After switching sign-in in one of those tools, the previous account's numbers can show for up to 1–2 minutes before the cache expires. Fixing it means reading each tool's credentials before every cache hit; say if you want that.\n\nThe dashboard preview is running again at http://127.0.0.1:4174."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":255544,"output_tokens":1377,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1377,"cache_read_input_tokens":255544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfpt2ZrhsMZ7AzEDrMCbx","type":"assistant","uuid":"a7ff2f56-acea-44ed-a678-1c5162dcffde","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:52:43.996Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
