{"parentUuid":"16074f31-59fb-4b4d-bf6e-bfdaffb27524","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpu73dXzL3fmd88fneqN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The push worked as `thyaravind` (the repo's git user), so I'll create the PR with that account's gh token for this one command, without switching your active account."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":262371,"output_tokens":1661,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":105},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1661,"cache_read_input_tokens":262371,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfpu73GwzhDNprnCoJkyc","type":"assistant","uuid":"6f7f07f4-b766-4a6c-a5ff-0023b43054eb","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:06:40.072Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"6f7f07f4-b766-4a6c-a5ff-0023b43054eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpu73dXzL3fmd88fneqN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AXoRE1tomPWdcJHwwZXfNJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git log -1 --format=%B > /dev/null && GH_TOKEN=\"$(gh auth token --user thyaravind)\" gh pr create --base main --head usage-dashboard-cli --title \"Add the local usage dashboard and @sub-set/usage CLI (SET-1)\" --body-file - <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nPilot for [SET-1](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-1/pilot-a-reusable-usage-status-dashboard): a local dashboard for AI subscription usage, packaged as a CLI.\n\n- **`@subset/usage`** (private): the usage contract (schema v1), read-only provider readers, local history, and the shared Svelte dashboard view.\n  - Readers: Codex/ChatGPT via app-server, Claude (status-line snapshots plus the live OAuth usage read), Cursor team (Admin API) and personal (desktop sign-in), Factory Droid, Amp, Devin, Antigravity, and Pi/OpenCode/omp/Hermes stored logins.\n- **`apps/usage`** (private): the standalone UI, covering the dashboard, settings, account dialogs, collector setup, and a first-run local sign-ins question.\n- **`@sub-set/usage`** (`packages/usage-cli`, public, not yet published): `subset-usage serve|status|collect`.\n  - Bundled with rolldown; Node 22 or later; no runtime dependencies.\n  - The server binds to 127.0.0.1 only, and every API call needs an `X-Subset-Request` header.\n  - `status` writes nothing.\n  - Collectors call a stable shim, one per configuration.\n- **Release**: `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`, modelled on Superfunctions. A `usage-v<version>` tag checks out and verifies that tag, then checks, builds, tests, packs, and publishes with `NPM_TOKEN`.\n  - `scripts/resolve-release-tag.mjs` refuses a version or name mismatch.\n  - `scripts/check-workspaces.mjs` checks public packages against `release-packages.json`.\n- **Docs and rules**:\n  - AGENTS.md: local sign-ins exception, owner-directed on 2026-10-08.\n  - Root README and `docs/architecture.md`.\n  - Package READMEs, including the Superfunctions reuse review.\n- **Catalog**: usage moves from `planned` to `building`. `availableSurfaces` stays empty.\n\n## Review notes\n\n- Two review passes were addressed:\n  - History retention and identity-safe caches.\n  - Claude snapshot identity binding and the shared Antigravity collector.\n  - Configured-key precedence for Factory and Devin; workspace-aware harness merging.\n  - Codex reset idempotency.\n  - Serialized writes.\n- Known limitation: the Factory, personal Cursor, Devin, and Amp caches are keyed by account. After a sign-in switch, the previous account's values can show for up to 1–2 minutes.\n- **Reviewer confirmation needed:** the AGENTS.md exception covers Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, Hermes, and the Antigravity email. Local sign-ins stay off until the user answers the first-run question.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass.\n- `npm test` passes: 93 library tests and 36 CLI tests.\n- The packed tarball, installed into a scratch prefix, serves the page, refuses API calls without the guard header, and writes the collector shim.\n- Live local run against real accounts across all providers.\n- Not verified:\n  - npm publication (no tag pushed).\n  - The workflow on GitHub.\n  - Agent-host embedding.\n  - The first-run banner in a browser.\n  - The macOS menu-bar app ([SET-14](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-14/deliver-subset-usage-as-a-macos-menu-bar-app-tauri), backlog).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF","description":"Create PR using the thyaravind account","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":262371,"out