0:46.547Z","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"910bc529-27ed-4b69-ba9c-43f1554f823d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c774b04c-c23f-4473-b206-32f54e0c9d68","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GMTiDzWRT8s4pW5E656VhV","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (29.3KB). Full output saved to: /Users/serro/.claude/projects/-Users-serro-Documents-dev-n-subset/ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe/tool-results/b6x1963m9.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n   34229 threads.txt\n### T0 kody-ai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:377 outdated=False\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\nStale state bug: openAdd is the only place that resets `storedLogin`, so submitAdd sends a radio choice from a previous harness after the user switches `newProvider`. Switching from Pi 'chatgpt' to omp creates an omp profile without an entryId that reads the first stored ChatGPT row, and switching from OpenCode 'opencode-go' to Pi submits an unsupported login kind that the server rejects, while the `!storedLogin` check leaves the submit button enabled. Clear `storedLogin` whenever `newProvider` changes (e.g. in an $effect), or validate it against `storedLogins[newProvider]` before submitting.\nTalk to Kody by mentioning @kody\nWas this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Ko\n### T1 kody-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:449 outdated=False\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\nSymlink clobbering in writeSettings: renaming the temp file over the settings path replaces a symlinked settings.json (e.g. ~/.claude/settings.json linked from a dotfiles repo) with a regular file, so installing, uninstalling, or migrating a collector silently detaches the dotfiles copy and uninstall restores the status line only in the detached copy. Resolve the real path with realpath first and write the temp file next to the resolved target before renaming.\nTalk to Kody by mentioning @kody\nWas this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.\n&#8203;\n&#8203;\n### T2 kody-ai packages/usage/src/codex.ts:161 outdated=False\n...\n</persisted-output>\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5b1ae97e-ae8a-4681-900a-a8fefc73a5ce","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:30:46.696Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"   34229 threads.txt\n### T0 kody-ai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:377 outdated=False\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\nStale state bug: openAdd is the only place that resets `storedLogin`, so submitAdd sends a radio choice from a previous harness after the user switches `newProvider`. Switching from Pi 'chatgpt' to omp creates an omp profile without an entryId that reads the first stored ChatGPT row, and switching from OpenCode 'opencode-go' to Pi submits an unsupported login kind that the server rejects, while the `!storedLogin` check leaves the submit button enabled. Clear `storedLogin` whenever `newProvider` changes (e.g. in an $effect), or validate it against `storedLogins[newProvider]` before submitting.\nTalk to Kody by mentioning @kody\nWas this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Ko\n### T1 kody-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:449 outdated=False\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\nSymlink clobbering in writeSettings: renaming the temp file over the settings path replaces a symlinked settings.json (e.g. ~/.claude/settings.json linked from a dotfiles repo) with a regular file, so installing, uninstalling, or migrating a collector silently detaches the dotfiles copy and uninstall restores the status line only in the detached copy. Resolve the real path with realpath first and write the temp file next to the resolved target before renaming.\nTalk to Kody by mentioning @kody\nWas this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.\n&#8203;\n&#8203;\n### T2 kody-ai packages/usage/src/codex.ts:161 outdated=False\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\nUnsettled promise in consumeCodexResetCredit: pending requests reject only on the child's 'exit' event or a stdin write-callback error, while the 'error' handler swallows spawn failures and the timeout only calls child.kill(), so a missing or non-executable codex binary hangs POST /api/profiles/:id/reset with the dialog stuck on 'Resetting…'. Reject all pending requests on child 'error' and on timeout, matching readCodexProfile.\n```typescript\nconst rejecters = new Set void>();\n// in request(): rejecters.add(reject);\nconst failAll = () => { for (const r of rejecters) r(new Error('Codex app-server closed.')); };\nchild.on('error', failAll);\nchild.on('exit', failAll);\nconst timer = set\n### T3 coderabbitai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:16 outdated=False\n**📐 Maintainability & Code Quality** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**Declare `phosphor-svelte` in `apps/usage/package.json`.**\n`App.svelte` imports `phosphor-svelte` directly, but the app manifest does not declare it. Add the existing `3.1.0` version.\n### T4 coderabbitai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:475 outdated=False\n**🔒 Security & Privacy** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**State in the first-run banner that the usage endpoints are undocumented.**\nThe repository exception requires that \"the UI must name these tools and say the endpoints are undocumented.\" This banner is where the user first decides on local sign-ins. It names the tools, but it does not say that the endpoints are undocumented. Only the Settings panel (line 586) says this, and the user can answer the first-run question without opening Settings. Add the same disclosure to the banner text.\nBased on learnings: \"the UI must name these tools and say the endpoints are undocumented.\"\n_Source: Learnings_\n### T5 coderabbitai packages/usage-cli/README.md:13 outdated=False\n**🎯 Functional Correctness** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**Separate current installation instructions from post-release commands.**\nThe README says `@sub-set/usage` is not published, but the **Use** section starts with `npx` and a global registry install. Outside a workspace that already has the package, npm must fetch it remotely, so these commands cannot install this pilot yet. Show the tarball or repository installation path here. Label the registry commands as post-release instructions. ([docs.npmjs.com](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/npm-exec/?utm_source=openai))\n### T6 coderabbitai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:449 outdated=False\n**🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**Resolve symlinks before replacing the CLI settings file.**\n`writeSettings` writes a temporary file and then calls `rename(temporary, file)`. If `settings.json` is a symlink, `rename` replaces the link with a regular file. Users who manage `~/.claude/settings.json` or `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json` from a dotfiles repository often use such links. The consequences:\n- After `installCollector`, the dotfiles copy no longer receives the change. Later edits to the dotfiles copy no longer reach the CLI.\n- `uninstallCollector` and `migrateCollectors` use the same path, so they keep writing the detached regular file.\n`stat(file)` already follows the link to read the mode. Resolve the target the same way before you build the temporary path and call `rename`.\n### T7 coderabbitai packages/usage/README.md:29 outdated=False\n**🔒 Security & Privacy** | **🟠 Major** | **🏗️ Heavy lift**\n**Remove the credential-refreshing Claude Code status check.**\nThe Claude Code usage path runs `claude auth status` before reading usage. This command can refresh the stored token and change the user's sign-in during a dashboard read. Remove this command from the usage-read path and update this README paragraph so it describes only read-only credential access.\n_Source: Learnings_\n### T8 coderabbitai packages/usage/src/cursor-local.ts:64 outdated=False\n**🎯 Functional Correctness** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**Do not report $0 on-demand spend when Cursor gives no remaining amount.**\nIf `spendLimitUsage.individualRemaining` is missing or invalid, `individualRemaining` is `null`. Line 64 then still adds an \"On-demand spend\" balance of `0`. That balance has `kind: 'provider-reported-amount'`. The dashboard shows $0.00 as a provider value, but Cursor never reported it. The presentation layer's contract says \"They never invent provider data\".\nAdd the balance only when Cursor reports both values.\n### T9 coderabbitai packages/usage/src/index.ts:127 outdated=False\n**🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**Keep reader labels within the usage-status contract.**\n`isUsageStatus` rejects the complete status when an account label exceeds 80 characters. `packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts` can emit a 128-character label. `packages/usage/src/cursor.ts` accepts labels up to 120 characters and copies them into `UsageAccount`. A host that builds a status from either reader can therefore receive a status that the dashboard rejects.\nThe CLI already limits configured labels to 80 characters. Its 20-profile limit also prevents the claimed 21-account CLI status. The 50-account limit in `history.ts` applies only to stored history.\nMake every reader enforce the 80-character `UsageAccount.label` bound, or raise the validator bound only after every reader enforces the same larger bound.\n### T10 coderabbitai packages/usage/src/index.ts:189 outdated=False\n**🎯 Functional Correctness** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**Do not treat every `claude-code` account as a status-line snapshot.** With local sign-ins on, the server returns live `claude-code` accounts from `readClaudeOAuthUsage` (`source: 'Claude usage (local sign-in)'`). Both the agent text and the badge logic decide snapshot status from the provider alone. Decide it from the account source, or add an explicit field.\n- `packages/usage/src/index.ts#L189-L189`: add the \"last collected CLI snapshot, not a live provider read\" note only when `account.source` is a status-line snapshot.\n- `packages/usage/src/present.ts#L25-L25`: change `isSnapshotProvider` to check the account source. With that change, stale live Claude reads get the \"Stale\" warning, and `needsAttention` counts them.\n### T11 coderabbitai packages/usage/src/UsageDashboard.svelte:357 outdated=False\n**🎯 Functional Correctness** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**Key the upcoming-reset rows and alert rows by a unique window identity.**\nLine 357 builds row keys from `accountId` and the display title, `reset.window`. Line 623 keys alert rows by `item.window`. Display titles are not unique within one account:\n- **Antigravity:** an account may mix grouped buckets (`gemini-5h`, `3p-5h`) with an ungrouped key such as `Gemini Pro`. `windowGroups` then returns `null`, and both 5-hour buckets get the title \"5-hour usage\".\n- **Claude OAuth:** a scoped model slug that contains digits does not match `^seven_day_([a-z]+)$` in `windowTitle`. Its title then falls back to \"Weekly usage\", which is the same as `seven_day`.\nDuplicate keys in Svelte 5 `{#each}` blocks raise `each_key_duplicate` in development. In production builds, rows can be dropped or reused. `LimitItem` and the `nextResets` entries a\n### T12 pullfrog packages/usage/src/UsageDashboard.svelte:357 outdated=False\n[P1] Duplicate presentation titles crash the dashboard\nA Claude login read through Pi, OpenCode, omp, or Hermes can have both a general weekly window and a model-scoped weekly window, which `windowTitle()` currently renders as `Weekly usage` for both. This gives these rows identical keys; I reproduced `https://svelte.dev/e/each_key_duplicate` in the production build, leaving the dashboard with no account cards.\n### T13 pullfrog packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:219 outdated=False\n[P2] Matching plan types do not establish workspace identity\nTwo distinct ChatGPT Business workspaces can share the same email and plan, so this branch assigns both harness groups to one direct Codex owner and suppresses their cards. An end-to-end `status` reproduction showed separate 20% and 80% workspace cards without a direct profile, but only the direct profile's 10% card after adding it, with both harnesses incorrectly listed in `alsoIn`.\n### T14 pullfrog packages/usage/src/index.ts:190 outdated=False\n[P2] Include provider balances in the text fallback\n`usageText()` never includes `account.balances`, so an Amp account with a valid $12.50 credit balance and $5 daily free allowance produces `ok ... usage unavailable`. This loses Amp's entire useful result for text-only hosts and also hides other providers' paid-credit balances; include the labeled amounts and currencies in the fallback and test a balance-only account.\n### T15 cubic-dev-ai AGENTS.md:72 outdated=False\nP1: The host calls `claude auth status` before checking whether local sign-ins are enabled, and that command can refresh the Claude Code token. Gate this read on the setting and ensure it cannot refresh tokens, or the documented opt-in/no-refresh guarantee is false.\n### T16 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/codex.ts:167 outdated=False\nP1: A failed `account/rateLimits/read` becomes `creditId = null`, but the following call still redeems without an ID, letting Codex choose a different reset. Reject the read error before consuming.\n### T17 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/history.ts:40 outdated=False\nP2: `__proto__` is an accepted account ID, so `series[account.id]` resolves to `Object.prototype` and the window write pollutes the process prototype. Initialize `series` with `Object.create(null)`; otherwise this account is omitted from returned history.\n```suggestion\n  const series: UsageHistory['series'] = Object.create(null);\n```\n### T18 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/present.ts:38 outdated=False\nP2: Claude OAuth keeps digits in model-scoped window IDs (for example, `Sonnet 4.5` becomes `seven_day_sonnet45`), but this regex only matches letters. These windows all become `Weekly usage`, producing indistinguishable titles and duplicate upcoming-reset keys; include digits or derive the model name from `window.label`.\n### T19 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/local-auth.ts:68 outdated=False\nP2: The `maxBytes` guard runs only after `response.text()` buffers the full body, and `text.length` is not a byte count. A large upstream response can exhaust the local server’s memory before rejection; stream the body and stop once its byte count exceeds the limit.\n```suggestion\n    const maxBytes = options.maxBytes ?? 512 * 1024;\n    const reader = response.body?.getReader();\n    const chunks: Uint8Array[] = [];\n    let size = 0;\n    if (reader) {\n      try {\n        while (true) {\n          const { done, value } = await reader.read();\n          if (done) break;\n          size += value.byteLength;\n          if (size > maxBytes) {\n            await reader.cancel().catch(() => {});\n            return { status: response.status, json: null, retryAfterMs };\n          }\n          chunks.push(value);\n        }\n      } finally { reader.releaseLock(); }\n    }\n    const text = new TextDecoder().\n### T20 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts:40 outdated=False\nP2: `gemini-constructor` passes `safeName`, but this lookup returns the inherited `Object` constructor as `durationMinutes`; JSON serialization omits it and `isUsageStatus()` rejects the whole status. Check `Object.hasOwn` before returning the mapped span.\n### T21 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/present.ts:267 outdated=False\nP2: `activityGrid` builds local-calendar days with fixed 24-hour intervals, so DST shifts midnight and mislabels or drops activity; its membership check also assumes every local day is exactly 24 hours. Generate boundaries with calendar-day arithmetic and compare each start to the next local midnight.\n### T22 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/codex.ts:97 outdated=False\nP2: `earliestExpiry` includes redeemed credits, while the displayed credit list and `nextResetCredit` exclude them, so the dashboard can report an ineligible credit as next. Filter to available credits before calculating it.\n```suggestion\n    const expiry = Array.isArray(resetCredits?.credits)\n      ? resetCredits.credits.map(object)\n        .filter((item): item is RecordValue => !!item && (item.status === undefined || item.status === 'available'))\n        .map((item) => timestamp(item.expiresAt))\n        .filter((item): item is string => item !== null)\n        .sort()[0] ?? null\n      : null;\n```\n### T23 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:175 outdated=False\nP2: This queue only serializes writes within one `createAccounts` instance. Two `serve` processes can read the same profile list and replace it with stale results, silently losing an account addition or removal; coordinate profile mutations across processes or detect and retry stale writes.\n### T24 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/present.ts:142 outdated=False\nP2: A valid window can have unknown `usedPercent` but known `remainingPercent`, yet this skips it from `highest` (and `needsAttention` and display tone also read only `usedPercent`); `limitAlerts` already derives usage from remaining. Derive `100 - remainingPercent` when used is unknown so the dashboard still ranks and warns on known low or exhausted quotas.\n### T25 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/present.ts:206 outdated=False\nP2: This labels every zero-use window without a reset as not yet started, but only Factory establishes that meaning; Codex and Claude keep missing reset times as partial data. Their cards therefore report unavailable reset times as “Starts on first use”; make this label conditional on the provider's semantics.\n### T26 cubic-dev-ai apps/usage/package.json:10 outdated=False\nP2: The `serve` script fails on Windows because npm runs it through `cmd.exe`, which does not support this POSIX environment-assignment syntax. Set `SUBSET_USAGE_WEB_DIR` with a cross-platform launcher or a Node wrapper so Windows users can start the dashboard.\n### T27 cubic-dev-ai scripts/check-workspaces.mjs:57 outdated=False\nP2: Duplicate release slugs pass this check, but the tag resolver selects only the first matching target, making another package impossible to release by tag. Assert that each slug is unique.\n```suggestion\n  assert.match(target.slug, /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$/);\n  assert.equal(releaseTargets.filter((entry) => entry.slug === target.slug).length, 1);\n```\n### T28 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/index.ts:190 outdated=False\nP2: Text-only results label Amp’s balance-only account `usage unavailable` and omit Factory’s extra-usage balance. Include `account.balances` in this summary so clients relying on `text` receive those provider-reported amounts.\n### T29 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/stored-logins.ts:191 outdated=False\nP2: An empty ChatGPT window such as `{}` is emitted, then this line marks the account `ok` and clears errors. Skip unusable windows and report incomplete responses as `partial`.\n### T30 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:447 outdated=False\nP2: Resolve `file` with `canonical` before deriving the temporary path and renaming; otherwise this replaces a symlinked settings file instead of updating its target.\n### T31 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/stored-logins.ts:94 outdated=False\nP2: OpenCode API-key entries under `openai` or `anthropic` can be treated as ChatGPT or Claude subscriptions and sent to their usage endpoints. Use `key` only for OpenCode Go; read OAuth `access` for subscription logins.\n```suggestion\n    const token = kind === 'opencode-go' ? text(entry.access) ?? text(entry.key) : text(entry.access);\n```\n### T32 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/README.md:23 outdated=False\nP2: This blanket statement contradicts the supported personal Cursor reader above, which reports provider-reported usage windows from the local Cursor sign-in. Limit the warning to what the team API cannot access and clarify that the opt-in local reader is separate.\n```suggestion\n**The Cursor team API does not support personal subscriptions.** It reads only configured team-member spending; the opt-in local Cursor reader above separately reads personal usage. Anthropic API billing, Claude Enterprise analytics, Gemini API billing, context-window percentages, and local session token counts are not implemented as subscription quota sources.\n```\n### T33 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor-local.ts:31 outdated=False\nP2: On Windows, this reader cannot reach Cursor's sign-in: it selects the Linux database path and invokes `/usr/bin/sqlite3`, then treats the resulting error as a missing token. Add the Windows app-data path and a supported SQLite reader, or explicitly report Windows as unsupported.\n### T34 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:465 outdated=False\nP2: Reject outstanding requests in `consumeCodexResetCredit` on child `error` and timeout; otherwise a missing `codex` binary leaves this awaited reset request pending.\n### T35 cubic-dev-ai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:631 outdated=False\nP2: Clear `storedLogin` when this radio changes `newProvider`; otherwise `submitAdd` can reuse a login selected for the previous harness.\n### T36 cubic-dev-ai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:475 outdated=False\nP2: Disclose in this first-run banner that these tools' usage endpoints are undocumented; users can opt in without opening Settings, where the disclosure currently lives.\n```suggestion\nSubset can show live usage from the logins Claude, Factory Droid, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes keep locally, and the Antigravity account email. Tokens are read, never changed or sent anywhere except the usage endpoints those tools use. Their makers do not document these endpoints, and the endpoints may change. You can change this in Settings.\n```\n### T37 cubic-dev-ai docs/architecture.md:22 outdated=False\nP2: This says refresh does not query Claude Code, but opt-in local sign-ins trigger `readClaudeOAuthUsage()` during refresh. Clarify that snapshot timestamps stay unchanged while the live Claude read may still run.\n### T38 cubic-dev-ai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:500 outdated=False\nP2: The empty-state CTA bypasses the active-sign-in guard on the app-bar Add button. While a sign-in is pending, it lets users start another ChatGPT add flow that the server rejects; apply the same guard here.\n### T39 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts:115 outdated=False\nP2: `sanitizeSnapshot` has already capped quota to 32 entries here, so `entries.length === 32` cannot distinguish a complete 32-window source from a truncated one. This marks complete capped profiles `partial`; track whether a 33rd valid bucket was dropped before setting this flag.\n### T40 cubic-dev-ai scripts/check-workspaces.mjs:51 outdated=False\nP2: This check only inspects `dependencies`. A public package can list a private workspace under `peerDependencies` or `optionalDependencies` and pass validation. Include those fields in the same check.\n```suggestion\n  for (const dependency of Object.keys({ ...manifest.dependencies, ...manifest.optionalDependencies, ...manifest.peerDependencies })) {\n```\n### T41 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:257 outdated=False\nP2: Native Windows installs cannot run the previous status-line command because `/bin/sh` is unavailable, so the collector stops rendering that status line. Use the platform's supported shell and command syntax, or explicitly disable/document collector chaining on Windows.\n### T42 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/README.md:47 outdated=False\nP2: This says Codex account email is discarded at the adapter boundary and never sent to the dashboard, but the Dashboard view section says the email appears under the plan, and `codex.ts` keeps it in the normalized account. Remove the discard and not-sent claims, or state that email is kept for display and omitted only from the agent text fallback.\n### T43 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/local-auth.ts:66 outdated=False\nP2: This ignores valid HTTP-date `Retry-After` values, causing the server to use its five-minute fallback instead of the provider’s requested cooldown. Parse both standard header formats before returning `retryAfterMs`.\n```suggestion\n    const seconds = retryAfter && /^\\d{1,6}$/.test(retryAfter.trim()) ? Number(retryAfter) : NaN;\n    const date = retryAfter ? Date.parse(retryAfter) : NaN;\n    const retryAfterMs = Number.isFinite(seconds) ? Math.min(seconds * 1000, 3_600_000)\n      : Number.isFinite(date) ? Math.max(0, Math.min(date - Date.now(), 3_600_000)) : null;\n```\n### T44 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/stored-logins.ts:169 outdated=False\nP2: `reloginRequired` is checked after `!token`, so a Hermes entry flagged for re-login without an access token is reported `unavailable` instead of `unauthorized`. Check the explicit flag first.\n```suggestion\n  if (entry.reloginRequired) return fail('stored_login_relogin', `${tool} needs you to sign in again.`, 'unauthorized');\n  if (!token) return fail('stored_login_unreadable', `${tool}'s stored login could not be read.`);\n```\n### T45 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/factory.ts:160 outdated=False\nP2: The 429 branch drops the provider's `Retry-After`, so the server always uses its fixed 5-minute cooldown. Attach `retryAfterMs: response.retryAfterMs` as the other readers do.\n```suggestion\n    if (response.status === 429) return { ...fail('factory_rate_limited', 'Factory is rate-limiting usage checks. Try again later.'), retryAfterMs: response.retryAfterMs } as UsageAccount;\n```\n### T46 cubic-dev-ai scripts/generate-provider-logos.mjs:29 outdated=False\nP2: This denylist misses active SVG constructs that would be injected through `{@html}` in `ProviderIcon.svelte`. It does not catch single-quoted `href='http...'`, `href=\"javascript:...\"`, ``, ``, or ``/`` that retarget `href`. Reject those patterns too, or allow only internal `#id` references.\n```suggestion\n  if (/]|]|]|\\son[a-z]+\\s*=|(?:xlink:)?href\\s*=\\s*[\"']?\\s*(?!#)|javascript:|data:/i.test(svg)) throw new Error(`${file} contains active or external content.`);\n```\n### T47 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor-local.ts:64 outdated=False\nP2: When `individualRemaining` is missing, this balance reports $0.00 spend as if the provider had reported it. Skip the balance when `individualRemaining` is null instead of defaulting to 0.\n```suggestion\n  if (individualLimit !== null && individualLimit > 0 && individualRemaining !== null) balances.push({ kind: 'provider-reported-amount', currency: 'USD', amount: Math.max(0, individualLimit - individualRemaining), label: 'On-demand spend', note: `Limit $${individualLimit.toFixed(2)}` });\n```\n### T48 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/amp.ts:49 outdated=False\nP2: Amp sign-in errors written to stderr are classified as generic `amp_failed`, so the account appears unavailable instead of signed out and loses its Fix action. Include stderr when classifying the command failure.\n### T49 cubic-dev-ai .github/workflows/publish-tag.yml:77 outdated=False\nP2: `npm publish` without `--tag` assigns the `latest` dist-tag, so a prerelease tag like `usage-v0.2.0-rc.1` would become the default install. Pass a dist-tag for prerelease versions, or reject prerelease tags in `resolve-release-tag.mjs`.\n### T50 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:224 outdated=False\nP2: `removeProfile` swallows the failure from `uninstallCollector`, then forgets the account anyway. The Claude Code or Antigravity status line keeps running a collector for an account that no longer exists. Fail the removal when the collector cannot be uninstalled, or surface the error to the user.\n```suggestion\n      await uninstallCollector(id);\n```\n### T51 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:250 outdated=False\nP2: A non-atomic write to `claude-identities.json` can corrupt it, and a corrupt file makes `claudeIdentities()` return `{}`. The identity-change guard then resets, so the previous account's snapshots show under the new sign-in. Write through a temporary file and `rename`, as `updateHistory` does, and serialize writes.\n### T52 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:83 outdated=False\nP2: A transient non-429 failure in `throttled` deletes the cached good account, so the dashboard loses values it showed a moment earlier. The same branch also drops the reuse window, so every poll re-calls the provider while it keeps failing. Keep the last good account on non-rate-limit errors and only delete the entry when there is no account to keep.\n### T53 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/claude.ts:67 outdated=False\nP2: For signed-out and non-subscription Claude directories, this keeps the previous snapshot's `windows` and `observedAt` while only changing `state`. The card can then show old quota next to \"Signed out\" or \"quota is unavailable\". Clear `windows` (and the reset data) in these branches, or state that the values are stale.\n### T54 cubic-dev-ai package.json:8 outdated=False\nP2: The root `engines.node` still allows Node 20.19, but the CLI this PR adds requires Node 22+ and the root `build`/`check`/`test` scripts now run it. Raise this to `>=22.13.0` to match the project requirement, and update the README's Node requirement too.\n```suggestion\n    \"node\": \">=22.13.0\"\n```\n### T55 cubic-dev-ai AGENTS.md:72 outdated=False\nP2: This exception list omits Amp, but the README says Amp usage is opt-in under local sign-ins and the server reads it regardless of that setting. Either add Amp here with owner direction or make the README and server gating match this list.\n### T56 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/test/profiles.test.mjs:354 outdated=False\nP2: This `assert.rejects` chains two `addProvider` calls, so it passes if the first, expected-to-succeed add fails with the same message. Await the first add separately, then assert that only the second one rejects.\n```suggestion\n  assert.ok(await accounts.addProvider({ provider: 'claude-code', label: 'Manual default', claudeConfigDir: defaultClaudeConfigDir }));\n  await assert.rejects(accounts.addProvider({ provider: 'claude-code', label: 'Again', claudeConfigDir: defaultClaudeConfigDir }), /already uses this config directory/);\n```\n### T57 cubic-dev-ai scripts/check-workspaces.mjs:53 outdated=False\nP2: This accepts public-to-public workspace dependencies, but the workspace rule above forces their range to `*`. `npm publish` ships that range unchanged, so consumers would float to any future version of the dependency. Require a pinned published range for public dependencies, or reject them until a real dependency needs one.\n### T58 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor.ts:154 outdated=False\nP2: Requiring `totalPages` and `totalMembers` to stay identical across all pages turns a legitimate mid-scan membership change into a `malformed_response` failure for the whole read. Consider tolerating drift in these counters, or re-reading from page 1 when they change.\n### T59 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:76 outdated=False\nP2: Concurrent status reads for the same account each call the undocumented live endpoint, because nothing dedupes in-flight reads. Store the pending promise per key in `liveCache` and return it to callers that arrive while the read is running.\n### T60 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor-local.ts:33 outdated=False\nP2: A failed state-database read (for example, `/usr/bin/sqlite3` missing or the DB unreadable) is reported as 'not signed in', which sends users to sign in again for no reason. Keep read failures distinct from an absent token, and report them as an unreadable state with a clear message.\n### T61 cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/scripts/build.mjs:13 outdated=False\nP2: `--check` passes whenever the old `dist/cli.mjs` and `web/` exist, so editing `src/` and packing without rebuilding ships stale code. Either run the build from `prepack`, or compare the artifact mtimes against `src/` and `packages/usage/dist` and fail whe","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/serro/.claude/projects/-Users-serro-Documents-dev-n-subset/ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe/tool-results/b6x1963m9.txt","persistedOutputSize":30021},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"910bc529-27ed-4b69-ba9c-43f1554f823d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
