7:07.892Z","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"78fb69aa-3d90-4fcb-8e27-69bd7ae3de75","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c774b04c-c23f-4473-b206-32f54e0c9d68","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AN5fbPgz7jsy8mYAZS6Hkw","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5c8e2df9-e1a6-47ad-9e9d-c7c0b3e94a38","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:37:08.063Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/docs/architecture.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":13,"newStart":13,"newLines":13,"lines":[" | Native delivery | Swift and platform APIs when required | Planned. Native permissions and views stay in native targets; share a stable data/operation contract where useful. |"," | Agent delivery | Structured result, optional registered view; separate local CLI/skill | Planned. Each host and the published CLI/skill require their own verification. |"," ","-The usage dashboard boundary is normalized per-source status and explicit read operations. Its sources are ChatGPT-signed-in Codex homes through the documented local app-server protocol, independently collected Claude Code/Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, authorized Cursor team-member spending through its official Admin API, and, only with the opt-in local sign-ins setting (see AGENTS.md), the stored sign-ins of Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app (personal plan usage), Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. Quota snapshots and spending caps remain distinct; API billing is not an implemented quota source. The local host runtime ships as the `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`packages/usage-cli`), which bundles `@subset/usage` and the built `apps/usage` view; a tag `usage-v<version>` runs `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`. The standalone host owns profile persistence and collector bindings, while the package owns normalization and source reads. Proposed consumers are a standalone web host, an Outright adapter, a local CLI and skill for shell-capable agents, and a registered view in an agent host. The PDF review boundary is document identity, page/annotation operations, and explicit export; web, native, product, and agent views may differ. No capability may import an app or a consuming product.","+The usage dashboard boundary is normalized per-source status and explicit read operations. Its sources are ChatGPT-signed-in Codex homes through the documented local app-server protocol, independently collected Claude Code/Antigravity CLI quota snapshots, authorized Cursor team-member spending through its official Admin API, Amp credit and allowance through the documented `amp usage` command, and, only with the opt-in local sign-ins setting (see AGENTS.md), the stored sign-ins of Claude Code, Factory Droid, the Cursor app (personal plan usage), Devin, Pi, OpenCode, omp, and Hermes. Quota snapshots and spending caps remain distinct; API billing is not an implemented quota source. The local host runtime ships as the `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`packages/usage-cli`), which bundles `@subset/usage` and the built `apps/usage` view; a tag `usage-v<version>` runs `.github/workflows/publish-tag.yml`. The standalone host owns profile persistence and collector bindings, while the package owns normalization and source reads. Proposed consumers are a standalone web host, an Outright adapter, a local CLI and skill for shell-capable agents, and a registered view in an agent host. The PDF review boundary is document identity, page/annotation operations, and explicit export; web, native, product, and agent views may differ. No capability may import an app or a consuming product."," "," ## Decisions and gates"," "," 1. Keep the directory a static build. Choose Cloudflare service, data residency, auth, cost, and rollback only when a pilot requires server-side work. No deployment is implied by this plan."," 2. Inspect current `superfunctions-dev` implementation, manifest, and docs before selecting authfn, billfn, datafn, filefn, mcpfn, plugfn, apifn, uifn, or observability. Record the package/version used and gaps in each capability README. No Superfunctions dependency has been selected for a pilot yet.","-3. For usage, Codex uses one `CODEX_HOME` per sign-in with manual live reads. Claude Code and Antigravity use allowlisted status-line snapshots with explicit per-account collector bindings, and a Claude account can be bound to its own `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`; refresh does not advance snapshot observation times or query those providers. Cursor team profiles select an exact member ID and reference a server environment credential, never a browser token. The host provides account operations and keeps credentials out of rendered status. Live multi-account sign-ins, installed CLI compatibility, Cursor authorization, and external host behavior still need verification before any availability claim. See [the usage README](../packages/usage/README.md) and [SET-1 and its linked planning documents](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-1/pilot-a-reusable-usage-status-dashboard).","+3. For usage, Codex uses one `CODEX_HOME` per sign-in with manual live reads. Claude Code and Antigravity use allowlisted status-line snapshots with explicit per-account collector bindings, and a Claude account can be bound to its own `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`; refresh does not advance snapshot observation times. With local sign-ins on, Claude accounts are also read live from the stored sign-in during refresh. Cursor team profiles select an exact member ID and reference a server environment credential, never a browser token. The host provides account operations and keeps credentials out of rendered status. Live multi-account sign-ins, installed CLI compatibility, Cursor authorization, and external host behavior still need verification before any availability claim. See [the usage README](../packages/usage/README.md) and [SET-1 and its linked planning documents](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SET-1/pilot-a-reusable-usage-status-dashboard)."," 4. For PDF review, compare browser and SwiftUI/PDFKit behavior against the existing POC, then choose the first standalone surface based on annotation fidelity, file access, export, and permissions. Do not transfer POC code without an audit."," 5. Keep catalog `availableSurfaces` empty until the actual artifact and route pass release checks. A published CLI/skill and a hosted agent view are separate claims. A localhost browser page is not an embedded agent view."," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage-cli/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":13,"newStart":8,"newLines":20,"lines":[" "," Requires Node.js 22 or later."," ","+Until the first release, install from the repository:","+"," ```sh","-npx @sub-set/usage            # open the dashboard","-npm install -g @sub-set/usage # or install the subset-usage command","-subset-usage serve --port 4174 --no-open","-subset-usage status           # current usage as JSON, read-only","+npm ci && npm run build                     # at the repository root","+cd packages/usage-cli && npm pack           # builds and writes sub-set-usage-<version>.tgz","+npm install -g ./sub-set-usage-*.tgz        # installs the subset-usage command","+subset-usage                                # open the dashboard","+subset-usage status                         # current usage as JSON, read-only"," ```"," ","+After a release is published, the registry commands work too: `npx @sub-set/usage`, or `npm install -g @sub-set/usage`.","+","+Collectors and status-line chaining use a POSIX shell script, so they are supported on macOS and Linux; reading the Cursor app sign-in is not supported on Windows.","+"," | Command | What it does |"," | --- | --- |"," | `serve` (default) | Starts the dashboard on `127.0.0.1` (port 4174, or the next free port) and opens it. `--port <n>` requires that port; `--no-open` skips the browser. Ctrl-C stops it. |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":7,"newStart":20,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Claude and Antigravity collectors do not log in, extract tokens, read credential stores, or query undocumented endpoints. Independent snapshot files prevent one slot from overwriting another; labels alone do not establish distinct upstream identity. Authenticate each CLI environment with the intended account and bind the correct collector to it. Switching an upstream login requires reviewing that binding. Live multi-account authentication for these providers has not been verified."," ","-**Personal Cursor subscription quota is not supported.** The team API does not authorize reading unrelated personal subscriptions. Anthropic API billing, Claude Enterprise analytics, Gemini API billing, context-window percentages, and local session token counts are not implemented as subscription quota sources.","+**The Cursor team API does not read personal subscriptions.** It reads only configured team-member spending; the opt-in local Cursor reader above separately reads the personal plan of the Cursor app's own sign-in. Anthropic API billing, Claude Enterprise analytics, Gemini API billing, context-window percentages, and local session token counts are not implemented as subscription quota sources."," "," ## Local sign-ins (opt-in)"," "]},{"oldStart":44,"oldLines":7,"newStart":44,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," The view shows provider-reported used percentage and reset time per returned limit window. Remaining percentage is labeled as a calculation from reported usage. Codex's response-level `ordinaryUsageAllowed` is preserved separately: explicit `false` means `blocked`, even when quota percentages are positive or reset times have elapsed. Missing permission remains unavailable, never inferred from quota. Per-bucket `rateLimitReachedType` and `spendControlReached` are retained even when a bucket has no windows; the five known reached-limit reasons are allowlisted, and unknown or malformed access fields produce partial data. Aggregate permission and per-bucket restrictions remain distinct. These fields were verified against the generated non-experimental protocol of installed Codex CLI 0.159.3 without reading credentials or account state."," ","-Banked reset count, earliest known expiry, and per-credit details appear only when supplied. Missing observations and partial responses remain visible. Account email and opaque credit IDs are discarded at the adapter boundary. Observation time is captured when app-server returns. The view treats an observation older than five minutes as stale and updates freshness every 30 seconds independently of successful refreshes. Refresh is manual in the package; the standalone host can also refresh on an interval. The text-only fallback likewise includes source, observation time, freshness, calculation qualifiers, access denials, and sanitized failure details.","+Banked reset count, earliest known expiry, and per-credit details appear only when supplied. Missing observations and partial responses remain visible. Opaque credit IDs are discarded at the adapter boundary. The account email is kept for display and left out of the agent text fallback; the ChatGPT workspace ID is used only inside the host to match logins and is removed before status is returned. Observation time is captured when app-server returns. The view treats an observation older than five minutes as stale and updates freshness every 30 seconds independently of successful refreshes. Refresh is manual in the package; the standalone host can also refresh on an interval. The text-only fallback likewise includes source, observation time, freshness, calculation qualifiers, access denials, and sanitized failure details."," "," The read request is local and read-only. `agentUsageResult(status)` yields structured data, a text fallback, and a trusted view ID. The isolated Outright SET-1 integration registers a read-only Codex MCP tool with McpFn and an inspector for this view. Its tool and browser behavior require separate host checks before claiming availability. Account connection is an explicit operation in the standalone local host. Reset redemption is the one provider mutation, behind a confirmation; purchases and other mutations are not exposed."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/docs/architecture.md","/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage-cli/README.md","/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset/packages/usage/README.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"78fb69aa-3d90-4fcb-8e27-69bd7ae3de75","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
