{"parentUuid":"5770622c-678e-4669-8532-e5a4e0cfdb93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpwjZX7EDqKWVk8ZuZD7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":996,"cache_read_input_tokens":406298,"output_tokens":2247,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":41},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":996,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":406298,"cache_creation_input_tokens":996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":996},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7346,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfpwjZBmSfs2eAQ2kZ8eq","attributionSkill":"use-skillplane","type":"assistant","uuid":"a82082be-1214-412b-84ab-6e82d9a82fc3","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:41:14.669Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"a82082be-1214-412b-84ab-6e82d9a82fc3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpwjZX7EDqKWVk8ZuZD7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran one review round on PR #6 and pushed a single fix commit, `c1b0718`, to https://github.com/21nCo/subset/pull/6. GitHub's PR view still showed the old head when I checked; the branch itself has the new commit.\n\n**Scope:** at head `f0d5777` I fetched 75 open review threads (cubic 60, CodeRabbit 9, kody 3, pullfrog 3), the review bodies and comments, and the check results. Two checks had something to report: the SonarCloud quality gate failed (50 annotations), and Socket Security came back neutral with its scan skipped. The rest passed or were skipped by the bots.\n\n**Fixed:**\n- **Dashboard crash (pullfrog's top finding):** two Claude weekly windows could get the same title, which crashed the production build. Titles now come from the window labels, including Claude logins read through Pi/OpenCode/omp/Hermes, and every list row is keyed by window rather than title.\n- **Workspace merging:** Codex's documented `account/read` reports the ChatGPT workspace ID, so harness logins now merge into a ChatGPT card only when the workspace IDs match. The ID is used inside the server and never returned in status.\n- **Codex resets:**\n  - A reset request now ends with an error if the Codex app-server can't start or times out, instead of hanging.\n  - It no longer spends a reset when reading the available credits failed.\n  - The earliest expiry now ignores credits already used.\n- **Provider readers:**\n  - Responses are read with a size cap instead of being buffered whole.\n  - Retry-After dates are understood, and Factory's 429 now passes its Retry-After on.\n  - OpenCode API keys are no longer treated as ChatGPT or Claude subscriptions; \"sign in again\" is reported before \"unreadable\"; incomplete ChatGPT windows show as partial.\n  - Personal Cursor no longer shows an invented $0 spend, and an unreadable state database is no longer reported as \"signed out\". Reading the Cursor app sign-in now reports \"unsupported\" on Windows.\n  - Amp sign-in errors printed to stderr now show as signed out.\n  - Factory reports a missing limits group as missing data, not \"unsupported\".\n  - A signed-out Claude card no longer shows old quota.\n  - Account labels are capped at 80 characters, and an account ID of `__proto__` can no longer corrupt usage history.\n- **Dashboard details:**\n  - The text-only fallback now includes balances, so Amp's credit appears.\n  - Live and snapshot Claude reads are told apart by source.\n  - Remaining-only windows are ranked; \"Starts on first use\" shows for Factory only; the activity heatmap stays aligned across daylight-saving changes.\n- **CLI:**\n  - Settings writes follow a symlinked `settings.json` instead of replacing the link.\n  - Removing an account fails (and keeps it) if its collector can't be uninstalled.\n  - Concurrent reads of the same account share one provider call.\n  - `claude-identities.json` is written atomically.\n  - The previous status line runs through the platform's shell.\n  - `--web-dir` replaces the POSIX-only env syntax in the dev script.\n- **Release and checks:**\n  - Prerelease tags publish under npm's `next` tag, and the publish job installs with `--ignore-scripts`.\n  - Packing now rebuilds first.\n  - The workspace check rejects duplicate release slugs and public packages that depend on workspace packages.\n  - The SVG logo check is stricter; the generated logos are unchanged.\n  - The minimum Node version is now 22, and the verify workflow uses Node 22.\n- **UI and docs:**\n  - The add-account dialog clears the previous harness's login choice, and the empty-state \"Add\" button is guarded during sign-in.\n  - Pins are capped at 50.\n  - The first-run banner says the endpoints are undocumented.\n  - Six doc corrections; `phosphor-svelte` is declared and `vite.config.ts` is type-checked.\n- **Test fixes:** 7 test-quality findings; 4 tests updated for the intended behaviour changes.\n\n**Not changed:**\n- **`claude auth status` (3 threads):** I judged these invalid. It's Claude Code's own documented command; Claude Code may refresh its own token there, but Subset never refreshes or writes tokens, and snapshot accounts need it even with local sign-ins off. Overrule me if you read the AGENTS.md rule differently.\n- **Amp in the AGENTS.md exception:** invalid in my view. Amp runs its documented `amp usage` command and doesn't read stored credentials.\n- **Keeping last good values on transient errors:** left as is, on purpose. AGENTS.md asks for read failures to be shown rather than old values.\n- **Cursor redirect error code:** redirects are still refused; only the reported error code differs, and fetch can't tell the two apart.\n- **Not attempted:**\n  - Locking profile writes across two `serve` processes (a cross-process design change).\n  - Tolerating Cursor team member-count drift mid-scan (it's a deliberate consistency check).\n  - Sonar's style warnings: cognitive complexity, nested ternaries, `await` in loops.\n  - The neutral Socket Security check (its scan was skipped, so nothing to act on).\n\n**Verification:**\n- 107 library and 38 CLI tests pass, including 14 new library regression tests and 2 new CLI tests. `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass, and `npm pack` works with the rebuild step.\n- Against the old head, 12 of the 14 new library tests fail and one hangs, as do both new CLI tests. The email-validation test also passes on old code, so the Sonar regex fix is proven by inspection only. The workspace matching has no automated test; I checked it against your real accounts, where the dashboard still shows the same 10 cards.\n- **Not yet verified:**\n  - Whether SonarCloud's gate now passes (I targeted the regex and the sort, which most likely caused its Security and Reliability failures).\n  - CI on the new commit.\n  - Re-reviews by the bots.\n  - Windows, beyond reporting it as unsupported.\n\n**Convergence:** this was a single run, so no record carries over between runs and trends across runs are unknown. Of 75 threads, 66 are fixed, 5 invalid and 4 not attempted. The pass was routine; no repeat-failure gate applied. No thread was replied to or resolved.\n\nOne review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":996,"cache_read_input_tokens":406298,"output_tokens":2247,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":41},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":996,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":406298,"cache_creation_input_tokens":996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":996},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfpwjZBmSfs2eAQ2kZ8eq","attributionSkill":"use-skillplane","type":"assistant","uuid":"f196fb11-d0f7-4a56-9522-cd5684161268","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:41:28.522Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
