{"parentUuid":"e958268f-952a-40a7-ba9d-7b73b6e8982e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1b1e40cf-cb04-422f-98ab-09f48cb3a5f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BqyjFkH4nPkPc8nYsmsre4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t### U0 OLD coderabbitai packages/usage/README.md:29 outdated=False replies=0\n2\t**🔒 Security & Privacy** | **🟠 Major** | **🏗️ Heavy lift**\n3\t**Remove the credential-refreshing Claude Code status check.**\n4\tThe Claude Code usage path runs `claude auth status` before reading usage. This command can refresh the stored token and change the user's sign-in during a dashboard read. Remove this command from the usage-read path and update this README paragraph so it describes only read-only credential access.\n5\t_Source: Learnings_\n6\t### U1 OLD coderabbitai packages/usage/src/index.ts:141 outdated=False replies=0\n7\t**🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n8\t**Keep reader labels within the usage-status contract.**\n9\t`isUsageStatus` rejects the complete status when an account label exceeds 80 characters. `packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts` can emit a 128-character label. `packages/usage/src/cursor.ts` accepts labels up to 120 characters and copies them into `UsageAccount`. A host that builds a status from either reader can therefore receive a status that the dashboard rejects.\n10\tThe CLI already limits configured labels to 80 characters. Its 20-profile limit also prevents the claimed 21-account CLI status. The 50-account limit in `history.ts` applies only to stored history.\n11\tMake every reader enforce the 80-character `UsageAccount.label` bound, or raise the validator bound only after e\n12\t### U2 OLD pullfrog packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:229 outdated=False replies=0\n13\t[P2] Matching plan types do not establish workspace identity\n14\tTwo distinct ChatGPT Business workspaces can share the same email and plan, so this branch assigns both harness groups to one direct Codex owner and suppresses their cards. An end-to-end `status` reproduction showed separate 20% and 80% workspace cards without a direct profile, but only the direct profile's 10% card after adding it, with both harnesses incorrectly listed in `alsoIn`.\n15\t### U3 OLD cubic-dev-ai AGENTS.md:72 outdated=False replies=0\n16\tP1: The host calls `claude auth status` before checking whether local sign-ins are enabled, and that command can refresh the Claude Code token. Gate this read on the setting and ensure it cannot refresh tokens, or the documented opt-in/no-refresh guarantee is false.\n17\t### U4 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:175 outdated=False replies=0\n18\tP2: This queue only serializes writes within one `createAccounts` instance. Two `serve` processes can read the same profile list and replace it with stale results, silently losing an account addition or removal; coordinate profile mutations across processes or detect and retry stale writes.\n19\t### U5 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor-local.ts:None outdated=True replies=0\n20\tP2: On Windows, this reader cannot reach Cursor's sign-in: it selects the Linux database path and invokes `/usr/bin/sqlite3`, then treats the resulting error as a missing token. Add the Windows app-data path and a supported SQLite reader, or explicitly report Windows as unsupported.\n21\t### U6 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:None outdated=True replies=0\n22\tP2: Native Windows installs cannot run the previous status-line command because `/bin/sh` is unavailable, so the collector stops rendering that status line. Use the platform's supported shell and command syntax, or explicitly disable/document collector chaining on Windows.\n23\t### U7 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:89 outdated=False replies=0\n24\tP2: A transient non-429 failure in `throttled` deletes the cached good account, so the dashboard loses values it showed a moment earlier. The same branch also drops the reuse window, so every poll re-calls the provider while it keeps failing. Keep the last good account on non-rate-limit errors and only delete the entry when there is no account to keep.\n25\t### U8 OLD cubic-dev-ai package.json:None outdated=True replies=0\n26\tP2: The root `engines.node` still allows Node 20.19, but the CLI this PR adds requires Node 22+ and the root `build`/`check`/`test` scripts now run it. Raise this to `>=22.13.0` to match the project requirement, and update the README's Node requirement too.\n27\t```suggestion\n28\t    \"node\": \">=22.13.0\"\n29\t```\n30\t### U9 OLD cubic-dev-ai AGENTS.md:72 outdated=False replies=0\n31\tP2: This exception list omits Amp, but the README says Amp usage is opt-in under local sign-ins and the server reads it regardless of that setting. Either add Amp here with owner direction or make the README and server gating match this list.\n32\t### U10 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor.ts:159 outdated=False replies=0\n33\tP2: Requiring `totalPages` and `totalMembers` to stay identical across all pages turns a legitimate mid-scan membership change into a `malformed_response` failure for the whole read. Consider tolerating drift in these counters, or re-reading from page 1 when they change.\n34\t### U11 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor.ts:123 outdated=False replies=0\n35\tP3: With `redirect: 'error'`, fetch rejects on a redirect instead of returning a 3xx response, so this check never runs. A redirect is reported as `request_failed` rather than `redirect_rejected`. Map the fetch rejection to `redirect_rejected` in the catch path, or remove the dead check.\n36\t### U12 NEW kody-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:269 outdated=False replies=0\n37\tLost update: the serialized write merges `{ ...current, ...identities }`, where `identities` is the full map read at line 123, so stale values for other profiles overwrite newer values written by a concurrent status() call. If call B records a sign-in change for profile P while call A is in progress, A's later write restores P's old email; the next refresh then detects an email change, resets `since` to Date.now(), hides valid snapshots as 'claude_identity_changed', and may attribute old snapshots to the wrong account. Track the profile IDs this call changed and merge only those entries over `current`.\n38\t```javascript\n39\t// Only entries this read changed; others may have been updated by a concurrent read.\n40\tconst updates = Object.fromEntries([...changedIdentityIds].map((id) => [id, identities[id]\n41\t### U13 NEW kody-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:85 outdated=False replies=0\n42\tInconsistent results for concurrent callers: `if (inFlight.has(key)) return inFlight.get(key);` returns the reader's raw result, so the 429 fallback to `entry.account` runs only for the caller that started the read. When refreshes overlap and the provider returns 429, the second caller receives the rate-limited error with no windows, and the dashboard flickers to an empty or error card despite cached values. Store a promise in `inFlight` that wraps both the read and the cache/cooldown logic so all callers share the post-processed result.\n43\t```javascript\n44\tif (inFlight.has(key)) return inFlight.get(key);\n45\tconst pending = (async () => {\n46\t  const result = await read();\n47\t  const limited = result.errors?.some((error) => /rate_limited$/.test(error.code));\n48\t  if (limited) {\n49\t    liveCache.set(key, { ...en\n50\t### U14 NEW kody-ai packages/usage/src/history.ts:54 outdated=False replies=0\n51\tType safety loss: `Object.create(null)` returns `any`, which collapses the union and infers `windows` as `any` instead of `Record>`. The compiler then stops checking `windows[key]`, `points.push(...)`, and the assignment back into `series`, violating the ban on `any`. Add an explicit type annotation, as lines 41 and 44 already do.\n52\tKody rule violation: [Disallow \\`any\\` type usage](https://app.kodus.io/settings/code-review/global/kody-rules/5ba5ce8d-2e90-425b-8ca3-6019f927f489?teamId=c7d4a17c-c2c8-426a-9c23-3048fd1d53b9)\n53\t```typescript\n54\tconst windows: Record> = series[account.id] ?? Object.create(null);\n55\t```\n56\t### U15 NEW kody-ai packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts:119 outdated=False replies=0\n57\tLost truncation flag: normalize() reads `quota_truncated` from `data = sanitizeSnapshot(profile, input)` (line 99), but sanitizeSnapshot rebuilds the result with only `plan_tier` and `quota` and cannot re-truncate an already-sanitized 32-bucket snapshot, so the stored flag is always dropped. With the old `entries.length >= MAX_WINDOWS` check removed, an Antigravity source with more than 32 buckets now reports 'ok' instead of 'partial' and never shows the 'at most 32 windows are retained' warning. The new test misses this because its envelope uses `snapshot`/`capturedAt` instead of `data`/`observedAt`, causing readSnapshotProfile to return snapshot_mismatch. Preserve the flag by copying `own(raw, 'quota_truncated') === true` in sanitizeSnapshot or by reading it from the raw `input` in norma\n58\t### U16 NEW pullfrog packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts:119 outdated=False replies=0\n59\t[P2] Preserve the truncation marker across sanitization passes\n60\t`normalize()` checks `quota_truncated` only after calling `sanitizeSnapshot()`, which drops an existing marker when the already-truncated payload contains exactly 32 buckets. I reproduced a 33-bucket input through `captureSnapshot()` and `readSnapshotProfile()`: both reported `ok`, with only 32 windows and no warning, silently hiding omitted quota.\n61\t### U17 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/test/server.test.mjs:45 outdated=False replies=0\n62\tP2: The readiness wait now sits outside the `try`/`finally`, so a readiness timeout or failure leaves the spawned server running and never removes the temp directory. Move the `try {` above this loop so the `finally` kills the child on any failure.\n63\t### U18 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/test/review-round.test.mjs:93 outdated=False replies=0\n64\tP2: This conditional assertion can pass without checking `state`. The snapshot is fresh, so assert `observedAt` is set and then assert the state unconditionally.\n65\t```suggestion\n66\t  assert.ok(read.observedAt);\n67\t  assert.equal(read.state, 'ok');\n68\t```\n69\t### U19 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:446 outdated=False replies=0\n70\tP2: A dangling `settings.json` symlink still gets replaced: `canonical()` falls back to the link path when `realpath()` fails. Resolve the symlink destination even when its target file is absent before renaming.\n71\t### U20 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/present.ts:30 outdated=False replies=0\n72\tP2: Rounding before threshold checks can make the account indicator disagree with the low-limit alerts: 15.04% remaining is marked at least 85% used here, but `limitAlerts` emits no alert. Keep the derived value precise and round only for display.\n73\t```suggestion\n74\t  window.usedPercent ?? (window.remainingPercent === null ? null : 100 - window.remainingPercent);\n75\t```\n76\t### U21 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/present.ts:172 outdated=False replies=0\n77\tP2: When a window reports only `remainingPercent`, used mode still returns `window.usedPercent`, so the dashboard shows “Unknown” even though `usedOf` can derive usage. Return the derived value in used mode and mark it calculated.\n78\t```suggestion\n79\t  return { value: mode === 'used' ? usedOf(window) : value, calculated: mode === 'used' ? window.usedPercent === null || calculated : calculated, tone: usedTone(usedOf(window)) };\n80\t```\n81\t### U22 NEW cubic-dev-ai scripts/generate-provider-logos.mjs:19 outdated=False replies=0\n82\tP2: The new `ACTIVE_SVG` check blocks the SVG `` element but not HTML embedded-media breakout elements, so `` (and ``, ``, ``) passes validation even though the comment above promises \"no scripts, event handlers, embedded documents or images\". These bodies are injected via `{@html body}` inside `` in `packages/usage/src/ProviderIcon.svelte`, and an HTML parser treats `` as a foreign-content breakout: it becomes a real HTML image that loads `src`, i.e. exactly the category of active content the check is meant to reject. Add the HTML media/embed elements to the blocked element list (verified: `ACTIVE_SVG.test('')` returns false today).\n83\t```suggestion\n84\tconst ACTIVE_SVG = /<(?:script|foreignObject|image|iframe|embed|object|video|audio|canvas|img|source|link|meta|base|a|set|animate\\w*|style)\\b|\\s\n85\t### U23 NEW cubic-dev-ai package.json:8 outdated=False replies=0\n86\tP2: This range advertises Node 22.0–22.12 as supported, below the project’s Node `>=22.13.0` requirement. Raise it to `>=22.13.0` so npm rejects unsupported runtimes.\n87\t```suggestion\n88\t    \"node\": \">=22.13.0\"\n89\t```\n90\t### U24 NEW cubic-dev-ai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:124 outdated=False replies=0\n91\tP2: At 50 pinned accounts, adding another pin silently does nothing because `slice(0, 50)` discards the newly appended ID. Retain the newest 49 existing pins before appending the new one.\n92\t```suggestion\n93\t    pinned = pinned.includes(id) ? pinned.filter((item) => item !== id) : [...pinned.slice(-49), id];\n94\t```\n95\t### U25 NEW cubic-dev-ai scripts/resolve-release-tag.mjs:96 outdated=False replies=0\n96\tP2: A stable version with a hyphen in its build metadata is incorrectly tagged `next`, so it will not become the default npm install. Check for a prerelease hyphen only before the `+` build metadata.\n97\t```suggestion\n98\t  npm_tag: version.split('+', 1)[0].includes('-') ? 'next' : 'latest',\n99\t```\n100\t### U26 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:265 outdated=False replies=0\n101\tP2: The merge lets this call's stale in-memory identities overwrite newer on-disk entries written by a concurrent status read. Persist only the keys this call changed, not the whole in-memory map.\n102\t### U27 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:79 outdated=False replies=0\n103\tP2: Concurrent waiters bypass the stale-account fallback on a 429, so simultaneous `/api/status` calls can return different quota data. Await the shared read and apply the same rate-limit fallback before returning.\n104\t```suggestion\n105\t  if (inFlight.has(key)) {\n106\t    const result = await inFlight.get(key);\n107\t    return result.errors?.some((error) => /rate_limited$/.test(error.code)) ? entry?.account ?? result : result;\n108\t  }\n109\t```\n110\t### U28 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/index.ts:41 outdated=False replies=0\n111\tP2: `agentUsageResult` returns `structuredContent: status` as-is, so a `workspaceId` on the status reaches the agent. Strip `workspaceId` inside `agentUsageResult`, or enforce the removal in this helper, rather than relying on every host to do it.\n112\t### U29 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/index.ts:204 outdated=False replies=0\n113\tP2: The text fallback reports unlimited Codex credits as `0 credits`. Render `unlimited` when `note === 'Unlimited'` and drop that note from the parenthetical, matching the dashboard's `amountText`.\n114\t```suggestion\n115\t    const balances = (account.balances ?? []).map((balance) => `${balance.label}: ${balance.note === 'Unlimited' ? 'unlimited' : balance.currency === 'USD' ? `USD ${balance.amount.toFixed(2)}` : `${balance.amount} credits`}${balance.note && balance.note !== 'Unlimited' ? ` (${balance.note})` : ''}`);\n116\t```\n117\t### U30 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/test/server.test.mjs:56 outdated=False replies=0\n118\tP3: The `in use` check runs on `'exit'`, which can fire before the child's stderr has been fully read, so the retry can be skipped. Listen for `'close'` instead, which fires after stdio has closed.\n119\t```suggestion\n120\t      child.once('close', () => { clearTimeout(timer); if (/in use/.test(stderr) && attempt < 3) resolve(false); else reject(new Error(`Server exited before readiness. ${stderr}`)); });\n121\t```\n122\t### U31 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/test/review-round.test.mjs:78 outdated=False replies=0\n123\tP3: A wall-clock threshold makes this test flaky on slow or loaded CI runners. Keep the functional `isEmail` assertions and drop the timing assertion, or put the ReDoS guard in a dedicated benchmark.\n124\t### U32 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor.ts:17 outdated=False replies=0\n125\tP3: The 80-character bound is hardcoded here, duplicating `MAX_ACCOUNT_LABEL` from `index.ts`. Import `MAX_ACCOUNT_LABEL` and use it so the Cursor adapter cannot drift from the status contract.\n126\t### U33 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/index.ts:8 outdated=False replies=0\n127\tP3: `accountLabel` can split an emoji or other surrogate pair at the 80-unit boundary, leaving a lone surrogate in the label. Trim by code points instead, for example `[...value].slice(0, MAX_ACCOUNT_LABEL).join('')`, though this still counts code points rather than UTF-16 units, so it does not match the `text()` check exactly.\n128\t```suggestion\n129\texport const accountLabel = (value: string): string => [...value].slice(0, MAX_ACCOUNT_LABEL).join('');\n130\t```\n131\t### U34 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:27 outdated=False replies=0\n132\tP3: `--web-dir` with no value is silently ignored: when the flag is the last argument, `process.argv[webOption + 1]` is `undefined`, so the condition is false and the default (or `SUBSET_USAGE_WEB_DIR`) build is served with no warning. A dropped path argument in development then shows a stale build instead of failing.\n133\t```suggestion\n134\tconst webValue = webOption > 0 ? process.argv[webOption + 1] : undefined;\n135\tif (webOption > 0 && !webValue) { console.error('--web-dir needs a path argument.'); process.exit(2); }\n136\tconst web = resolve(webValue ?? process.env.SUBSET_USAGE_WEB_DIR ?? resolve(packageRoot, 'web'));\n137\t```\n138\t### U35 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/history.ts:54 outdated=False replies=0\n139\tP3: Annotate `windows` as `Record>`; `Object.create(null)` makes this expression `any` and disables checks for the mutations below.\n140\t"}]},"uuid":"db0592ae-90b6-4b70-b0a1-3639ff4e9f47","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:22:05.218Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-serro-Documents-dev-n-subset/ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe/scratchpad/pr6/r2/unresolved.txt","content":"### U0 OLD coderabbitai packages/usage/README.md:29 outdated=False replies=0\n**🔒 Security & Privacy** | **🟠 Major** | **🏗️ Heavy lift**\n**Remove the credential-refreshing Claude Code status check.**\nThe Claude Code usage path runs `claude auth status` before reading usage. This command can refresh the stored token and change the user's sign-in during a dashboard read. Remove this command from the usage-read path and update this README paragraph so it describes only read-only credential access.\n_Source: Learnings_\n### U1 OLD coderabbitai packages/usage/src/index.ts:141 outdated=False replies=0\n**🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**\n**Keep reader labels within the usage-status contract.**\n`isUsageStatus` rejects the complete status when an account label exceeds 80 characters. `packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts` can emit a 128-character label. `packages/usage/src/cursor.ts` accepts labels up to 120 characters and copies them into `UsageAccount`. A host that builds a status from either reader can therefore receive a status that the dashboard rejects.\nThe CLI already limits configured labels to 80 characters. Its 20-profile limit also prevents the claimed 21-account CLI status. The 50-account limit in `history.ts` applies only to stored history.\nMake every reader enforce the 80-character `UsageAccount.label` bound, or raise the validator bound only after e\n### U2 OLD pullfrog packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:229 outdated=False replies=0\n[P2] Matching plan types do not establish workspace identity\nTwo distinct ChatGPT Business workspaces can share the same email and plan, so this branch assigns both harness groups to one direct Codex owner and suppresses their cards. An end-to-end `status` reproduction showed separate 20% and 80% workspace cards without a direct profile, but only the direct profile's 10% card after adding it, with both harnesses incorrectly listed in `alsoIn`.\n### U3 OLD cubic-dev-ai AGENTS.md:72 outdated=False replies=0\nP1: The host calls `claude auth status` before checking whether local sign-ins are enabled, and that command can refresh the Claude Code token. Gate this read on the setting and ensure it cannot refresh tokens, or the documented opt-in/no-refresh guarantee is false.\n### U4 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:175 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: This queue only serializes writes within one `createAccounts` instance. Two `serve` processes can read the same profile list and replace it with stale results, silently losing an account addition or removal; coordinate profile mutations across processes or detect and retry stale writes.\n### U5 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor-local.ts:None outdated=True replies=0\nP2: On Windows, this reader cannot reach Cursor's sign-in: it selects the Linux database path and invokes `/usr/bin/sqlite3`, then treats the resulting error as a missing token. Add the Windows app-data path and a supported SQLite reader, or explicitly report Windows as unsupported.\n### U6 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:None outdated=True replies=0\nP2: Native Windows installs cannot run the previous status-line command because `/bin/sh` is unavailable, so the collector stops rendering that status line. Use the platform's supported shell and command syntax, or explicitly disable/document collector chaining on Windows.\n### U7 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:89 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: A transient non-429 failure in `throttled` deletes the cached good account, so the dashboard loses values it showed a moment earlier. The same branch also drops the reuse window, so every poll re-calls the provider while it keeps failing. Keep the last good account on non-rate-limit errors and only delete the entry when there is no account to keep.\n### U8 OLD cubic-dev-ai package.json:None outdated=True replies=0\nP2: The root `engines.node` still allows Node 20.19, but the CLI this PR adds requires Node 22+ and the root `build`/`check`/`test` scripts now run it. Raise this to `>=22.13.0` to match the project requirement, and update the README's Node requirement too.\n```suggestion\n    \"node\": \">=22.13.0\"\n```\n### U9 OLD cubic-dev-ai AGENTS.md:72 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: This exception list omits Amp, but the README says Amp usage is opt-in under local sign-ins and the server reads it regardless of that setting. Either add Amp here with owner direction or make the README and server gating match this list.\n### U10 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor.ts:159 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: Requiring `totalPages` and `totalMembers` to stay identical across all pages turns a legitimate mid-scan membership change into a `malformed_response` failure for the whole read. Consider tolerating drift in these counters, or re-reading from page 1 when they change.\n### U11 OLD cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor.ts:123 outdated=False replies=0\nP3: With `redirect: 'error'`, fetch rejects on a redirect instead of returning a 3xx response, so this check never runs. A redirect is reported as `request_failed` rather than `redirect_rejected`. Map the fetch rejection to `redirect_rejected` in the catch path, or remove the dead check.\n### U12 NEW kody-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:269 outdated=False replies=0\nLost update: the serialized write merges `{ ...current, ...identities }`, where `identities` is the full map read at line 123, so stale values for other profiles overwrite newer values written by a concurrent status() call. If call B records a sign-in change for profile P while call A is in progress, A's later write restores P's old email; the next refresh then detects an email change, resets `since` to Date.now(), hides valid snapshots as 'claude_identity_changed', and may attribute old snapshots to the wrong account. Track the profile IDs this call changed and merge only those entries over `current`.\n```javascript\n// Only entries this read changed; others may have been updated by a concurrent read.\nconst updates = Object.fromEntries([...changedIdentityIds].map((id) => [id, identities[id]\n### U13 NEW kody-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:85 outdated=False replies=0\nInconsistent results for concurrent callers: `if (inFlight.has(key)) return inFlight.get(key);` returns the reader's raw result, so the 429 fallback to `entry.account` runs only for the caller that started the read. When refreshes overlap and the provider returns 429, the second caller receives the rate-limited error with no windows, and the dashboard flickers to an empty or error card despite cached values. Store a promise in `inFlight` that wraps both the read and the cache/cooldown logic so all callers share the post-processed result.\n```javascript\nif (inFlight.has(key)) return inFlight.get(key);\nconst pending = (async () => {\n  const result = await read();\n  const limited = result.errors?.some((error) => /rate_limited$/.test(error.code));\n  if (limited) {\n    liveCache.set(key, { ...en\n### U14 NEW kody-ai packages/usage/src/history.ts:54 outdated=False replies=0\nType safety loss: `Object.create(null)` returns `any`, which collapses the union and infers `windows` as `any` instead of `Record>`. The compiler then stops checking `windows[key]`, `points.push(...)`, and the assignment back into `series`, violating the ban on `any`. Add an explicit type annotation, as lines 41 and 44 already do.\nKody rule violation: [Disallow \\`any\\` type usage](https://app.kodus.io/settings/code-review/global/kody-rules/5ba5ce8d-2e90-425b-8ca3-6019f927f489?teamId=c7d4a17c-c2c8-426a-9c23-3048fd1d53b9)\n```typescript\nconst windows: Record> = series[account.id] ?? Object.create(null);\n```\n### U15 NEW kody-ai packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts:119 outdated=False replies=0\nLost truncation flag: normalize() reads `quota_truncated` from `data = sanitizeSnapshot(profile, input)` (line 99), but sanitizeSnapshot rebuilds the result with only `plan_tier` and `quota` and cannot re-truncate an already-sanitized 32-bucket snapshot, so the stored flag is always dropped. With the old `entries.length >= MAX_WINDOWS` check removed, an Antigravity source with more than 32 buckets now reports 'ok' instead of 'partial' and never shows the 'at most 32 windows are retained' warning. The new test misses this because its envelope uses `snapshot`/`capturedAt` instead of `data`/`observedAt`, causing readSnapshotProfile to return snapshot_mismatch. Preserve the flag by copying `own(raw, 'quota_truncated') === true` in sanitizeSnapshot or by reading it from the raw `input` in norma\n### U16 NEW pullfrog packages/usage/src/snapshots.ts:119 outdated=False replies=0\n[P2] Preserve the truncation marker across sanitization passes\n`normalize()` checks `quota_truncated` only after calling `sanitizeSnapshot()`, which drops an existing marker when the already-truncated payload contains exactly 32 buckets. I reproduced a 33-bucket input through `captureSnapshot()` and `readSnapshotProfile()`: both reported `ok`, with only 32 windows and no warning, silently hiding omitted quota.\n### U17 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/test/server.test.mjs:45 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: The readiness wait now sits outside the `try`/`finally`, so a readiness timeout or failure leaves the spawned server running and never removes the temp directory. Move the `try {` above this loop so the `finally` kills the child on any failure.\n### U18 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/test/review-round.test.mjs:93 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: This conditional assertion can pass without checking `state`. The snapshot is fresh, so assert `observedAt` is set and then assert the state unconditionally.\n```suggestion\n  assert.ok(read.observedAt);\n  assert.equal(read.state, 'ok');\n```\n### U19 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/accounts.mjs:446 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: A dangling `settings.json` symlink still gets replaced: `canonical()` falls back to the link path when `realpath()` fails. Resolve the symlink destination even when its target file is absent before renaming.\n### U20 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/present.ts:30 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: Rounding before threshold checks can make the account indicator disagree with the low-limit alerts: 15.04% remaining is marked at least 85% used here, but `limitAlerts` emits no alert. Keep the derived value precise and round only for display.\n```suggestion\n  window.usedPercent ?? (window.remainingPercent === null ? null : 100 - window.remainingPercent);\n```\n### U21 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/present.ts:172 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: When a window reports only `remainingPercent`, used mode still returns `window.usedPercent`, so the dashboard shows “Unknown” even though `usedOf` can derive usage. Return the derived value in used mode and mark it calculated.\n```suggestion\n  return { value: mode === 'used' ? usedOf(window) : value, calculated: mode === 'used' ? window.usedPercent === null || calculated : calculated, tone: usedTone(usedOf(window)) };\n```\n### U22 NEW cubic-dev-ai scripts/generate-provider-logos.mjs:19 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: The new `ACTIVE_SVG` check blocks the SVG `` element but not HTML embedded-media breakout elements, so `` (and ``, ``, ``) passes validation even though the comment above promises \"no scripts, event handlers, embedded documents or images\". These bodies are injected via `{@html body}` inside `` in `packages/usage/src/ProviderIcon.svelte`, and an HTML parser treats `` as a foreign-content breakout: it becomes a real HTML image that loads `src`, i.e. exactly the category of active content the check is meant to reject. Add the HTML media/embed elements to the blocked element list (verified: `ACTIVE_SVG.test('')` returns false today).\n```suggestion\nconst ACTIVE_SVG = /<(?:script|foreignObject|image|iframe|embed|object|video|audio|canvas|img|source|link|meta|base|a|set|animate\\w*|style)\\b|\\s\n### U23 NEW cubic-dev-ai package.json:8 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: This range advertises Node 22.0–22.12 as supported, below the project’s Node `>=22.13.0` requirement. Raise it to `>=22.13.0` so npm rejects unsupported runtimes.\n```suggestion\n    \"node\": \">=22.13.0\"\n```\n### U24 NEW cubic-dev-ai apps/usage/src/App.svelte:124 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: At 50 pinned accounts, adding another pin silently does nothing because `slice(0, 50)` discards the newly appended ID. Retain the newest 49 existing pins before appending the new one.\n```suggestion\n    pinned = pinned.includes(id) ? pinned.filter((item) => item !== id) : [...pinned.slice(-49), id];\n```\n### U25 NEW cubic-dev-ai scripts/resolve-release-tag.mjs:96 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: A stable version with a hyphen in its build metadata is incorrectly tagged `next`, so it will not become the default npm install. Check for a prerelease hyphen only before the `+` build metadata.\n```suggestion\n  npm_tag: version.split('+', 1)[0].includes('-') ? 'next' : 'latest',\n```\n### U26 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:265 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: The merge lets this call's stale in-memory identities overwrite newer on-disk entries written by a concurrent status read. Persist only the keys this call changed, not the whole in-memory map.\n### U27 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:79 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: Concurrent waiters bypass the stale-account fallback on a 429, so simultaneous `/api/status` calls can return different quota data. Await the shared read and apply the same rate-limit fallback before returning.\n```suggestion\n  if (inFlight.has(key)) {\n    const result = await inFlight.get(key);\n    return result.errors?.some((error) => /rate_limited$/.test(error.code)) ? entry?.account ?? result : result;\n  }\n```\n### U28 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/index.ts:41 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: `agentUsageResult` returns `structuredContent: status` as-is, so a `workspaceId` on the status reaches the agent. Strip `workspaceId` inside `agentUsageResult`, or enforce the removal in this helper, rather than relying on every host to do it.\n### U29 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/index.ts:204 outdated=False replies=0\nP2: The text fallback reports unlimited Codex credits as `0 credits`. Render `unlimited` when `note === 'Unlimited'` and drop that note from the parenthetical, matching the dashboard's `amountText`.\n```suggestion\n    const balances = (account.balances ?? []).map((balance) => `${balance.label}: ${balance.note === 'Unlimited' ? 'unlimited' : balance.currency === 'USD' ? `USD ${balance.amount.toFixed(2)}` : `${balance.amount} credits`}${balance.note && balance.note !== 'Unlimited' ? ` (${balance.note})` : ''}`);\n```\n### U30 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/test/server.test.mjs:56 outdated=False replies=0\nP3: The `in use` check runs on `'exit'`, which can fire before the child's stderr has been fully read, so the retry can be skipped. Listen for `'close'` instead, which fires after stdio has closed.\n```suggestion\n      child.once('close', () => { clearTimeout(timer); if (/in use/.test(stderr) && attempt < 3) resolve(false); else reject(new Error(`Server exited before readiness. ${stderr}`)); });\n```\n### U31 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/test/review-round.test.mjs:78 outdated=False replies=0\nP3: A wall-clock threshold makes this test flaky on slow or loaded CI runners. Keep the functional `isEmail` assertions and drop the timing assertion, or put the ReDoS guard in a dedicated benchmark.\n### U32 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/cursor.ts:17 outdated=False replies=0\nP3: The 80-character bound is hardcoded here, duplicating `MAX_ACCOUNT_LABEL` from `index.ts`. Import `MAX_ACCOUNT_LABEL` and use it so the Cursor adapter cannot drift from the status contract.\n### U33 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/index.ts:8 outdated=False replies=0\nP3: `accountLabel` can split an emoji or other surrogate pair at the 80-unit boundary, leaving a lone surrogate in the label. Trim by code points instead, for example `[...value].slice(0, MAX_ACCOUNT_LABEL).join('')`, though this still counts code points rather than UTF-16 units, so it does not match the `text()` check exactly.\n```suggestion\nexport const accountLabel = (value: string): string => [...value].slice(0, MAX_ACCOUNT_LABEL).join('');\n```\n### U34 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage-cli/src/server.mjs:27 outdated=False replies=0\nP3: `--web-dir` with no value is silently ignored: when the flag is the last argument, `process.argv[webOption + 1]` is `undefined`, so the condition is false and the default (or `SUBSET_USAGE_WEB_DIR`) build is served with no warning. A dropped path argument in development then shows a stale build instead of failing.\n```suggestion\nconst webValue = webOption > 0 ? process.argv[webOption + 1] : undefined;\nif (webOption > 0 && !webValue) { console.error('--web-dir needs a path argument.'); process.exit(2); }\nconst web = resolve(webValue ?? process.env.SUBSET_USAGE_WEB_DIR ?? resolve(packageRoot, 'web'));\n```\n### U35 NEW cubic-dev-ai packages/usage/src/history.ts:54 outdated=False replies=0\nP3: Annotate `windows` as `Record>`; `Object.create(null)` makes this expression `any` and disables checks for the mutations below.\n","numLines":140,"startLine":1,"totalLines":140}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e958268f-952a-40a7-ba9d-7b73b6e8982e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","use