{"parentUuid":"92199987-c920-498d-9c6f-4b925bf313d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfq14uWXPqWrFBDSrNDfY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SX7aBkAzcfKzZ3DZnNmqzF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -f /tmp/a1.json; cd /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset && git add -A && git diff --cached --check && git diff --cached --stat | tail -1 && git diff --cached package-lock.json | grep \"^[+-] \" | head -4 && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nFix second-round PR #6 review findings\n\n- Share the full post-processed read (cache and 429 fallback) with concurrent callers.\n- Persist only the Claude identities a read changed, so concurrent reads can't revert them.\n- Keep the Antigravity truncation marker through re-sanitization on read; the test\n  now uses the collector's real envelope and capture path.\n- Derived usage stays unrounded for thresholds and shows in used mode as calculated.\n- Agent results drop host-internal workspace IDs; text fallback says \"unlimited\".\n- Labels trim without splitting surrogate pairs; Cursor uses the shared label bound.\n- Settings writes follow dangling symlinks; --web-dir requires a value.\n- SVG check blocks HTML media breakout elements; build metadata no longer marks a\n  stable release as prerelease; newest pin replaces the oldest at 50.\n- Root Node floor 22.12 (Vite and rolldown requirement); history typing; server\n  test cleans up failed starts and reads stderr on close; no timing assertion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push 2>&1 | tail -1; git rev-parse HEAD origin/usage-dashboard-cli; GH_TOKEN=\"$(gh auth token --user thyaravind)\" gh pr view 6 --repo 21nCo/subset --json headRefOid -q .headRefOid","description":"Commit and push round-2 fixes once","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_c