{"parentUuid":"a5dff3ba-597a-4ee4-80a6-75a99ee2c824","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_019GKs5BqYmsMKufdeWh2QAX","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4ce58a1f-cf9f-486d-94fc-25b86f596ca2","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:25:39.328Z","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"4ce58a1f-cf9f-486d-94fc-25b86f596ca2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfq17Zc32gEV7V5sqsjGr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran a second review round on PR #6 and pushed one fix commit, `312c4ba`, to https://github.com/21nCo/subset/pull/6. Local, remote and PR head all match. The first push attempt was rejected with no reason shown; retrying the same commit worked. SonarCloud, which failed last round, now passes on the previous head (`c1b0718`).\n\n**Scope:** at `c1b0718` there were 36 unresolved threads: 25 new and 11 still open from round 1. The bots had resolved the other 63. Socket Security was again neutral (its scan skipped); all other checks passed or were skipped.\n\n**Fixed — three of these were bugs my round-1 fixes introduced:**\n- **Concurrent reads (from my fix):** callers waiting on a read already in progress skipped the rate-limit fallback, so overlapping refreshes could show an error card. The shared result now includes that fallback.\n- **Claude sign-in records (from my fix):** a status read could overwrite a newer sign-in record written by another read. Each read now writes back only the entries it changed.\n- **Antigravity bucket cap (from my fix):** the \"more than 32 buckets\" flag was lost when the snapshot was re-checked on read, so a capped snapshot showed as complete. My test missed it because it used the wrong snapshot file format. The flag now survives, and the tests use the real capture-and-read path.\n- **Remaining-only windows:** usage worked out from \"remaining\" was rounded before the 85% check, so the card warning and the alerts list could disagree. It's no longer rounded, and used mode now shows it, marked calculated.\n- **Agent output:** the agent result no longer includes the workspace ID, and the text fallback says \"unlimited\" instead of \"0 credits\".\n- **Labels:** trimming to 80 characters no longer splits an emoji, and the Cursor reader uses the shared limit.\n- **Settings and CLI flags:** settings writes follow a symlink even when its target doesn't exist yet, and `--web-dir` without a path is now an error.\n- **Logo check:** the SVG check now also blocks HTML media elements (`img`, `video` and similar), which can escape from inline SVG. The generated logos are unchanged.\n- **Releases:** a stable version with build metadata (`0.2.0+build-7`) no longer publishes under npm's `next` tag.\n- **Pins:** at 50, a new pin now replaces the oldest instead of silently doing nothing.\n- **Node version:** the root minimum is now 22.12, because Vite and rolldown require it.\n- **Tests and typing:** the history code is properly typed again; the server test cleans up after a failed start and reads its error output reliably; I removed a wall-clock timing check and a conditional assertion.\n\n**Already fixed (round 1):** the 80-character label limit, workspace matching, Windows Cursor and shell handling, and the earlier Node version thread.\n\n**Same decisions as round 1:**\n- **Invalid:** the three `claude auth status` threads; Amp in the AGENTS.md exception; keeping the last good values on errors; the Cursor redirect error code.\n- **Not attempted:** locking profile writes across two `serve` processes; tolerating member-count drift in Cursor team reads.\n\n**Verification:**\n- 109 library and 40 CLI tests pass, including 4 new regression tests. `npm run check`, `npm run build` and the packing step pass. The live dashboard shows the same 10 accounts.\n- Against the previous head, the new Antigravity-cap, remaining-only, emoji-trim and symlink tests all fail, so they catch the old bugs.\n- The two concurrency fixes have no automated test because that code isn't exported; I checked them by reading the code.\n- Not yet verified: CI and SonarCloud on the new commit, and the bots' re-reviews.\n\n**Convergence:** improving. Valid problems went from about 66 last round to 21 this round, and none remain open. Three problems came back as regressions of my round-1 fixes, each now on its second attempt — one more than the review skill's limit for routine fixes. The 7 invalid or not-attempted items are unchanged. No thread was replied to or resolved.\n\nOne review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":440799,"output_tokens":1416,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":423,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":440799,"cache_creation_input_tokens":423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":423},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfq17ZHgNEirH9EnH5XxC","attributionSkill":"use-skillplane","type":"assistant","uuid":"40596d9d-cd15-4f8c-bc63-d922e10ce43d","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:25:39.326Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
