{"parentUuid":"f8065ff1-8e7f-4ac0-9d8b-0fc9d76aa656","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14974883 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"abdeffa3-ef8b-4917-8a05-5beeb5a227ea","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:10:43.631Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14974883 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"abdeffa3-ef8b-4917-8a05-5beeb5a227ea","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Sdx6dj74UPj7d9fCgqVLRD","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1a5d76b9-3d39-494b-9c72-f7da243f6536","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:10:54.096Z","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
{"parentUuid":"1a5d76b9-3d39-494b-9c72-f7da243f6536","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqJJ4WMcLpUQvzLhcnFT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I pushed one commit, `09a0f5b`, to https://github.com/21nCo/subset/pull/6. It closes the workspace-identity issue pullfrog has been blocking approval on, and pins the release workflow's actions to fixed commits. Local and remote match; the PR page still showed `6ae3c9d` when I checked.\n\n**What was open:** no new review threads. Pullfrog's reviews of `312c4ba` and `6ae3c9d` both withheld approval over that same issue. CodeRabbit added a nitpick in a review body. All checks were green; Socket Security was neutral as before.\n\n**Fixed:**\n- **Harness accounts merged without proof (pullfrog):** pullfrog was right and I'd wrongly marked this fixed for two rounds. When either side had no ChatGPT workspace ID, the code still merged logins whose email and plan matched, which could join two separate Business workspaces.\n  - Logins now share a card only when the identity is proven. For ChatGPT that means the same email and the same workspace ID, both known; for Claude, which has no workspace, the same email.\n  - Plan matching and the \"only one workspace\" guess are gone; a login of unknown identity keeps its own card.\n  - Direct accounts use the same rule, so two direct ChatGPT profiles on one email with different workspaces no longer collide.\n- **Release workflow (CodeRabbit):** `actions/checkout` and `actions/setup-node` in `publish-tag.yml` are pinned to commit SHAs instead of `@v4`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- A new end-to-end test runs the CLI's `status` command against a fake Codex and a stored Pi login. It covers four cases: direct workspace unknown, harness workspace unknown, two different workspaces, and a true match.\n- Against `6ae3c9d` the test fails as pullfrog described (the Pi login merged by plan); now it passes.\n- `npm run check`, `npm run build` and all tests pass (109 library, 41 CLI).\n- Your real ChatGPT card still merges OpenCode, omp and Pi, so the stricter rule doesn't break genuine matches. The dashboard now shows 11 cards; the new one is a Claude account recently added to your profiles file, not something this change produced.\n- CI, SonarCloud and pullfrog's response to `09a0f5b` haven't been checked.\n\n**Other open threads:** the 13 carried over are unchanged. The skipped ones are the same seven as last round (four invalid, two not attempted, plus the `engines` thread).\n\n**Convergence:** improving. This issue had now gone through one incomplete fix and two rounds where I wrongly called it fixed, which trips the review skill's convergence limit. So instead of patching again, I first wrote down the rule it must satisfy and a reproduction on the old head, then fixed it in one change. The notes and the per-round history are in a scratch file (`scratchpad/pr6/ledger.md`), not the repo. No new problems or fix-induced regressions this round. No threads were replied to or resolved.\n\nThe preview is running again at http://127.0.0.1:4174.\n\nOne review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":703,"cache_read_input_tokens":488771,"output_tokens":1058,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":703,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1058,"cache_read_input_tokens":488771,"cache_creation_input_tokens":703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management