{"parentUuid":"6d84b0e7-78a0-417e-a92c-c040f2b2c71f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqNzk99u4ArQonas3XB8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both changes are made and verified locally; neither is committed yet. `npm run check`, `npm run build` and all 150 tests pass.\n\n**1. Usage logo from the landing page**\n- I took the Usage mark from the `subset-landing/usage` page in the 21n repo (`feat-subset-landing-site` branch, its `BrandMark.svelte`): the light, indigo and lime pixel bars. It now replaces the old three-bar logo in the dashboard header, as a new `apps/usage/src/BrandMark.svelte`.\n- One difference from the landing page: the top bar follows the text colour instead of fixed near-white, so it doesn't disappear in light mode. The other two bars keep the landing page's exact colours.\n- The landing page's favicons (`favicon.svg` and `favicon-32.png`) are in `apps/usage/public/` and linked from `index.html`. I also taught the server to serve `.png` files with the right content type.\n- In the running preview the mark renders in the header and both favicons load; I checked the dark theme in a screenshot.\n- This replaces your earlier `?logo-experiment=1–4` idea, so I didn't build that. Tell me if you still want it.\n\n**2. npm scope `@sub-set` → `@subset.dev`**\n- The publishable CLI package is now `@subset.dev/usage`, and no `@sub-set` references remain. Updated:\n  - `AGENTS.md`, `README.md` and `docs/architecture.md`.\n  - The package READMEs and the CLI's `package.json`.\n  - The `apps/usage` scripts, the root test script and `release-packages.json`.\n  - `scripts/check-workspaces.mjs` (it now requires `@subset.dev/*` for public packages).\n  - The lockfile.\n- Packing gives `subset.dev-usage-0.1.0.tgz`, and the release script resolves the tag `usage-v0.1.0` to `@subset.dev/usage`.\n- The private internal packages keep their `@subset/*` names, as AGENTS.md requires.\n\n**Check before releasing:**\n- **npm org:** `@subset.dev/usage` is a valid package name and nothing is published under it yet. I couldn't confirm a `subset.dev` org exists on npm, because npmjs.com blocks automated requests. The org needs to exist, and the org-wide `NPM_TOKEN` needs publish rights to it, or the first tagged publish will fail.\n- **Other places:** the earlier Linear backlog items and this session's PR descriptions may still mention `@sub-set`; I only changed files in this repo.\n\nThe preview is running with these changes at http://127.0.0.1:4174. Want me to commit and push this to the PR branch?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3591,"cache_read_input_tokens":520207,"output_tokens":1060,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3591,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1060,"cache_read_input_tokens":520207,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3591,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3591},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfqNzjgcmnGTzdeiJ9XZW","type":"assistant","uuid":"e42804d6-0e21-442d-9ae9-1bdb3fae3550","timestamp":"2026-10-08T20:12:33.299Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/subset","sessionId":"ccf55d8d-6176-4456-a8a3-555947c35bfe","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"usage-dashboard-cli","slug":"declarative-hopping-teapot"}
